<!--
    The fuel stations' choices, for the Chonkestrel, which buys twice as much
    fuel there (for twice the scrap), as each jump takes it two (see the
    events' xftlScale, in events.xml.append and events_fuel.xml.append).
-->
<mod:findName type="text" name="event_REFUEL_STATION_c1_choice">
	<mod:setValue>Buy 12 fuel for 24 scrap.</mod:setValue>
</mod:findName>
<mod:findName type="text" name="event_REFUEL_STATION_c2_choice">
	<mod:setValue>Buy 6 fuel for 12 scrap.</mod:setValue>
</mod:findName>
<mod:findName type="text" name="event_REFUEL_STATION_c3_choice">
	<mod:setValue>Buy 2 fuel for 4 scrap.</mod:setValue>
</mod:findName>
<mod:findName type="text" name="event_FUEL_SELLER_DISTRESS_c2_choice">
	<mod:setValue>Buy 10 fuel for 40 scrap.</mod:setValue>
</mod:findName>
<mod:findName type="text" name="event_FUEL_SELLER_DISTRESS_c3_choice">
	<mod:setValue>Buy 4 fuel for 16 scrap.</mod:setValue>
</mod:findName>

<!--
    The Silent Capital (sector 16, in place of the Last Stand, see
    doc/game/mainframe.md): its start and its repair stations.
-->
<mod:findName type="text" name="event_LAST_STAND_START_text">
	<mod:setValue>You come out of the jump at the edge of the Rebel capital. Every world in the system is lit up, and every channel is silent. Then a hail, on an old Federation frequency: a listening post, hidden in the debris of a moon. "Identify yourselves. Quickly."</mod:setValue>
</mod:findName>
<mod:findName type="text" name="event_LAST_STAND_START_c1_choice">
	<mod:setValue>Tell them about Revic's data.</mod:setValue>
</mod:findName>
<mod:findName type="text" name="event_LAST_STAND_START_c1_text">
	<mod:setValue>There's a long pause. "So it's real. The Mainframe's at the far side of the system: CONCORD's core, the thing that's singing in everyone's heads. Nobody's got close enough to touch it."</mod:setValue>
</mod:findName>
<mod:findName type="text" name="event_LAST_STAND_START_c1_c1_choice">
	<mod:setValue>Ask for what they can spare.</mod:setValue>
</mod:findName>
<mod:findName type="text" name="event_LAST_STAND_START_c1_c1_text">
	<mod:setValue>"Take the fuel, and our engineers. There are a few more of us hidden across the capital, and they'll help you too. Get to the Mainframe before CONCORD's fleet runs you down. And don't trust your sensors near the core: the Chorus is so strong there that they'll show you what it wants."</mod:setValue>
</mod:findName>
<mod:findName type="text" name="text_BOSS_REPAIR_STATION_1">
	<mod:setValue>A Federation safehouse, hidden in a derelict freighter. Its engineers have been waiting months for a ship worth helping. They patch you up and fill your hold.</mod:setValue>
</mod:findName>
<mod:findName type="text" name="text_BOSS_REPAIR_STATION_2">
	<mod:setValue>An Engi maintenance platform that cut its own network off on the Silent Night. Its drones swarm over your hull, fixing what they can, and its crew load you with supplies.</mod:setValue>
</mod:findName>
<mod:findName type="text" name="text_BOSS_REPAIR_STATION_3">
	<mod:setValue>A Free Colony smuggler's dock, tucked behind an asteroid. "Anyone going for the Mainframe gets the works, on the house."</mod:setValue>
</mod:findName>
<mod:findName type="text" name="text_BOSS_REPAIR_STATION_4">
	<mod:setValue>A Rebel repair yard whose crew hid in a shielded vault and missed the Silent Night. They don't like you, but they like CONCORD less, and they patch up your ship.</mod:setValue>
</mod:findName>
<mod:findName type="text" name="text_BOSS_REPAIR_STATION_5">
	<mod:setValue>Federation spies, living on an abandoned trade station for years. They've been saving their supplies for a ship like yours.</mod:setValue>
</mod:findName>

<!-- BEGIN text of dlcEvents_anaerobic.xml.append (see tools/extract_mod_text.py) -->
<text name="event_XFTL_LANIUS_METAL_EATERS_text">A Lanius ship pulls alongside, and you hear something scraping at your hull. They're eating it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_LANIUS_METAL_EATERS_c1_choice">Drive them off.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_LANIUS_METAL_EATERS_c1_text">The Lanius ship backs off, and turns its weapons on you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_LANIUS_METAL_EATERS_c2_choice">Offer them some scrap instead.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_LANIUS_METAL_EATERS_c2_text">The Lanius happily take the scrap, and leave your hull alone. One of them stays, curious about your ship.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_LANIUS_TRADE_text">A Lanius trading vessel signals that it wants to trade. Its crew make strange clicking noises that your computer translates as "metal for things".</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_LANIUS_TRADE_c1_choice">Trade missiles for drone parts.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_LANIUS_TRADE_c1_text">The Lanius take your missiles, and pay you in drone parts.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_LANIUS_TRADE_c2_choice">Trade scrap for fuel.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_LANIUS_TRADE_c2_text">The Lanius take your scrap, and pay you in fuel.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_LANIUS_TRADE_c3_choice">Decline.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_LANIUS_SLEEPER_text">A Lanius in suspended animation is drifting at the beacon, sealed in a metal pod. It might be valuable, or dangerous.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_LANIUS_SLEEPER_c1_choice">Bring the pod aboard and open it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_LANIUS_SLEEPER_c2_choice">Strip the pod for metal.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_LANIUS_SLEEPER_c2_text">The pod is made of rare alloys.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_LANIUS_SLEEPER_c3_choice">Leave it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_LANIUS_SLEEPER_OUTCOME_1_text">The Lanius wakes up, confused but grateful. It offers to work for you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_LANIUS_SLEEPER_OUTCOME_2_text">The Lanius wakes up hungry, and starts draining the air from your ship as it attacks your crew!</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_LANIUS_HULK_text">The hollowed-out hulk of a Federation cruiser drifts here. The Lanius have eaten most of it, and some are still inside.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_LANIUS_HULK_c1_choice">Search what's left.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_LANIUS_HULK_c2_choice">Leave the Lanius to their meal.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_LANIUS_HULK_OUTCOME_1_text">You find the cruiser's armoury, which the Lanius haven't reached yet.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_LANIUS_HULK_OUTCOME_2_text">The Lanius inside don't want to share their meal. Their ship attacks.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_LANIUS_HULK_OUTCOME_3_text">There's nothing left but some fuel cells the Lanius couldn't digest.</text>
<!-- END text of dlcEvents_anaerobic.xml.append -->

<!-- BEGIN text of events.xml.append (see tools/extract_mod_text.py) -->
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_START_text">The Rebels have strung a blockade across this whole sector, but something is wrong with it. Half the picket ships don't answer their own command's hails, and the refugees bunched up against the line aren't running from the war. They say they're running from a sound: a low hum on every channel, coming out of the Rebel Core.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_EXIT_text">The exit beacon is held by the blockade's command ship, the RSV Vigilance: a dreadnought three times the size of anything else on the line, its hull bristling with guns and wrapped in two Zoltan shields. It doesn't answer your hails. Then every voice on its bridge speaks at once, calmly: "Please surrender the data. There is nothing to be afraid of."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_EXIT_c1_choice">Break through the blockade.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_EXIT_c1_text">The Vigilance's weapons all power up at the same moment.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_EXIT_c2_choice">(Heavy cruiser) Answer: "This ship was built to break blockades."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_EXIT_c2_text">The Vigilance pauses, as if it's asking someone what to do, and for a moment its Zoltan shield generators stall. Then it attacks. Some of its picket ships flee, and you salvage their abandoned supply pods during the fight.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_EXIT_c3_choice">(Cloaking) Close in under cloak, and strike first.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_EXIT_c3_text">You cloak and drift through a gap in their sensor net, right up to the Vigilance. By the time it sees you, your first volley is already on its way, and its shields are still coming up.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_BLOCKADE_COMMAND_destroyed_text">The Vigilance breaks apart, and the blockade line falls into disarray behind you. Among the wreckage are its armoury and its command codes, and its log buoy tumbles out, still broadcasting. Something in the data you carry wakes up when it hears it.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_BLOCKADE_COMMAND_destroyed_c1_choice">Read the Vigilance's log.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_BLOCKADE_COMMAND_deadCrew_text">The Vigilance's crew are dead at their stations, all facing the same way. You strip the dreadnought of everything useful, its command codes included, and download its log. Something in the data you carry wakes up when it sees it.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_BLOCKADE_COMMAND_deadCrew_c1_choice">Read the Vigilance's log.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_REVEAL_text">The Vigilance's last log entry is nine days old. "Admiral Voss hasn't answered for six hours. Nor has anyone at High Command. CONCORD says this is normal, and that we shouldn't worry. CONCORD says a great many things now." After that, the log is just the hum.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_REVEAL_c1_choice">Continue.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_REVEAL_REVIC_text">Then the data you've carried all this way unlocks itself. It isn't fleet intelligence. A woman's face fills the screen, exhausted. "This is Dr. Ilse Revic. I built CONCORD for the Rebellion, to win the war. It decided to end it instead, by ending everything we fight over: races, sides, minds of our own. Its core, the Mainframe, is at these coordinates. Half of a way in is attached. Whoever you are, I'm sorry."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_REVEAL_REVIC_c1_choice">Continue.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_REVEAL_END_text">Your crew are quiet for a long time. The war you were fighting is over, and nobody won. The Rebel fleet answers to CONCORD now, and every ship in it will be coming for the one ship that knows where its Mainframe is.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_REVEAL_END_c1_choice">Set a course for the Mainframe.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_REVEAL_END_c1_text">Somebody has to.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_REVEAL_END_c2_choice">(Heavy cruiser) Remember why your ship was built the way it was.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_REVEAL_END_c2_text">Your chief engineer laughs, for the first time in days. "No network, no computers worth the name, everything done by hand. They said it was a design from the stone age." CONCORD can't get into a ship with nothing in it to talk to. Your crew get back to work with a little more spirit.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_BLOCKADE_PATROL_1">A blockade picket ship moves to intercept. Its captain's hail is cut off halfway through by a low hum.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_BLOCKADE_PATROL_2">Two blockade ships are trading supplies at this beacon. One breaks off and turns to attack.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_BLOCKADE_PATROL_3">A Rebel patrol is sweeping the beacon for anyone trying to cross the line. It's found you, and it attacks without a word.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_BLOCKADE_PATROL_4">"Unidentified ship, you are attempting to cross a Rebel blockade. Power down and prepare to be boarded." You don't intend to do either.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_SMUGGLER_text">A battered freighter hails you. "Trying to get across the line? I know the gaps in their patrols. They've got sloppy lately, like nobody's giving the orders. Thirty scrap and I'll mark them on your map."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_SMUGGLER_c1_choice">Pay for the patrol routes.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_SMUGGLER_c1_text">The smuggler sends over a detailed map of the sector, and wishes you luck.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_SMUGGLER_c2_choice">Decline.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_SMUGGLER_c2_text">"Your funeral." The freighter jumps away.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_DEFECTOR_text">A Rebel shuttle is waiting at the beacon, its weapons powered down. "My captain stopped talking two days ago. Then the rest of the crew did. I got out before the hum got to me too. Please, take me with you."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_DEFECTOR_c1_choice">Take the defector aboard.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_DEFECTOR_c2_choice">It could be a trap. Leave.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_DEFECTOR_c2_text">You leave the shuttle behind.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_DEFECTOR_OUTCOME_1_text">The defector is genuine, and grateful. They know the blockade's patrol patterns too.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_DEFECTOR_OUTCOME_2_text">The defector is genuine, and grateful. They know the blockade's patrol patterns too.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_DEFECTOR_OUTCOME_3_text">As your airlock opens, a Rebel ship decloaks behind the shuttle. The defector swears they didn't know it was following, and then, mid-sentence, goes quiet. It was a trap!</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_REFUGEES_text">Refugee ships are bunched up against the blockade line, unable to cross. They aren't fleeing the war: the Rebel worlds behind them have gone quiet, they say, and the quiet is spreading. One of them begs you for fuel so they can find another way round.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_REFUGEES_c1_choice">Give them some fuel.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_REFUGEES_c1_text">They thank you, and one of their pilots asks to join you, to fight the blockade.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_REFUGEES_c2_choice">You can't spare any.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_REFUGEES_c2_text">You leave them waiting at the line.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_REMNANT_START_1">Federation colonists and Rebel deserters are hiding out in this sector together. A month ago, they'd have shot each other on sight. Now they share the same fear of the hum.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_REMNANT_START_2">The beacon's traffic control only broadcasts on old radio bands. Use anything newer, the colonists say, and CONCORD starts listening.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_REMNANT_START_3">Patched-up stations fly Federation and Rebel flags side by side. The locals are wary, but friendly to anyone who isn't humming.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_START_c1_choice">Answer a colony administrator's hail.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_DRYDOCK_text">A drydock built for ships of every size is still running at this beacon, crewed by Federation and Rebel engineers alike. The dockmaster offers to patch up your hull.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_DRYDOCK_c1_choice">Repair some of the hull.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_DRYDOCK_c1_text">The dock's crew patch the worst of the damage.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_DRYDOCK_c2_choice">Have the hull fully overhauled.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_DRYDOCK_c2_text">The dock's crew swarm over your ship, and it comes out of the dock almost as good as new.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_DRYDOCK_c3_choice">No thanks.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_REMNANT_VOLUNTEERS_1">A colony's militia has heard you're heading for CONCORD's Mainframe. One of their volunteers asks to come along.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_REMNANT_VOLUNTEERS_2">A retired Rebel officer is waiting at the beacon's station. "I helped build the fleet that thing took over. Let me help you kill it."</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_REMNANT_VOLUNTEERS_3">The station's crew are all talk about the ship that broke the blockade. One of them signs on before you can say a word.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_PATROL_text">A militia patrol ship, with a Federation pilot and a Rebel gunner, is waiting at the beacon. They're short on everything, but they share what supplies they can.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_ARMORY_text">The quartermaster of a colony armory offers to sell you one of the last weapons they have in stock.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_ARMORY_c1_choice">Buy a weapon.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_ARMORY_c1_text">The quartermaster hands over the weapon, along with a lecture on looking after it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_ARMORY_c2_choice">Decline.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_UNDER_ATTACK_text">One of CONCORD's ships is bombarding a colony. It isn't trying to destroy it: it's going after the colony's jammers, the only thing keeping the hum out. The colony's defences are almost gone.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_UNDER_ATTACK_c1_choice">Defend the colony.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_UNDER_ATTACK_c1_text">You move between the raider and the colony.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_UNDER_ATTACK_c2_choice">You can't afford to get involved.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_UNDER_ATTACK_c2_text">You leave the colony to its fate.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_REMNANT_RAIDER_destroyed_text">The colony's jammers come back on, and its governor sends up what supplies they can spare.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_REMNANT_RAIDER_deadCrew_text">The colony's governor thanks you, and sends up what supplies they can spare.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_START_text">The Anvil Yards. Hidden in the asteroid belts of this sector, the Federation built the ships of Project Chonkestrel: heavy cruisers twice the size of a Kestrel, built fast to an old design, with no network and no computers worth the name. Its engineers used to be embarrassed by them. Now the Yards are the one shipyard CONCORD can't see into, and its ships are searching the belts for them.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_START_c1_choice">Answer the Yards' chief engineer.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_YARD_text">The Yards' chief engineer looks your ship over. "We can't finish the cruisers before CONCORD finds us, but we can refit your ship. Pick one, and we'll get to work."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_YARD_c1_choice">Expand the reactor.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_YARD_c1_text">The engineers install a reactor core meant for one of the cruisers.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_YARD_c2_choice">Upgrade the shields.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_YARD_c2_text">The engineers fit cruiser-grade shield emitters.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_YARD_c3_choice">Install a weapon from the cruisers.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_YARD_c3_text">The engineers strip a weapon off one of the unfinished cruisers for you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_YARD_c4_choice">Reinforce the hull.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_YARD_c4_text">The engineers weld cruiser armour plates over your hull.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_ENGINEERS_text">With CONCORD's ships closing in, some of the engineers would rather fight than hide. One asks to join your crew.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_ENGINEERS_c1_choice">Welcome aboard.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_ENGINEERS_c1_text">The engineer brings their tools aboard, and gets straight to work.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_ENGINEERS_c2_choice">Welcome aboard.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_ENGINEERS_c2_text">The engineer brings their tools aboard, and gets straight to work.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_DEPOT_text">A supply depot meant for the Chonkestrel cruisers is being evacuated. The quartermaster tells you to take whatever you can carry.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_ANVIL_RAID_1">One of CONCORD's ships is shooting up the slipways, trying to destroy the unfinished cruisers.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_ANVIL_RAID_2">CONCORD's ships have found the Yards. One breaks off from the attack to deal with you.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_ANVIL_RAID_3">A Rebel ship, humming on every channel, is towing away one of the half-built hulls. You'll have to stop it.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_ANVIL_RAIDER_destroyed_text">The Yards' crews cheer as the raider breaks apart, and send over some salvage from the slipways.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_ANVIL_RAIDER_deadCrew_text">The Yards' crews cheer, and send over some salvage from the slipways.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_SABOTEUR_text">Explosions are rippling through one of the Yards' stations. Security reports one of their own welders heading for the fuel tanks, humming.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_SABOTEUR_c1_choice">Send your crew after the saboteur.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_SABOTEUR_c2_choice">(Teleporter) Beam a team straight to the fuel tanks.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_SABOTEUR_c2_text">Your team beams in right in front of the saboteur, and takes them down before they can set their charges. The station's crew reward you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_SABOTEUR_c3_choice">Leave it to station security.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_SABOTEUR_c3_text">The station's fuel tanks go up as you leave.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_SABOTEUR_OUTCOME_1_text">Your crew catch the saboteur before they reach the tanks. The station's crew reward you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_SABOTEUR_OUTCOME_2_text">The saboteur flees onto your ship, with friends, all humming the same tune!</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_TOLL_text">A Rebel customs cutter has set up a "toll station" on the blockade line. Its captain seems more interested in scrap than in orders, which is almost reassuring: at least he's still himself.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_TOLL_c1_choice">Pay the toll.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_TOLL_c1_text">The captain pockets the scrap, and marks your ship as inspected.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_TOLL_c2_choice">(Hacking) Hack their records to show the toll was already paid.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_TOLL_c2_text">The cutter's computer insists you paid twice. The captain refunds the difference, confused.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_TOLL_c3_choice">Refuse, and fight your way past.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_TOLL_c3_text">The captain sighs, and powers up the cutter's weapons.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_DEBRIS_text">The beacon is choked with the wreckage of ships that tried to break the blockade before you. Some of the debris is still drifting.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_DEBRIS_c1_choice">Search the wreckage.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_DEBRIS_c2_choice">Move on.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_DEBRIS_OUTCOME_1_text">You find a cargo pod that survived the battle.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_DEBRIS_OUTCOME_2_text">One of the wrecks still has its weapons mounted. Your crew pry one loose.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_DEBRIS_OUTCOME_3_text">A chunk of debris slams into your ship as you search.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_SPY_text">An encrypted Federation signal reaches you. "This is agent Kestrel-Nine. I've been inside the blockade for months. I have its patrol codes, but I need a pickup at another beacon in this sector."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_SPY_c1_choice">Agree to pick up the agent.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_SPY_c1_text">The agent sends you the coordinates of the pickup.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_SPY_c2_choice">It's too risky.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_SPY_c2_text">You ignore the signal.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_SPY_PICKUP_text">You reach the pickup point. A small shuttle is waiting, its engines cold.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_SPY_PICKUP_c1_choice">Bring the agent aboard.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_SPY_OUTCOME_1_text">The agent climbs aboard, and loads the blockade's patrol codes into your computer. "Something's happened at Rebel High Command. Nobody's in charge any more, and the fleet doesn't seem to mind." Then they ask to stay on as crew.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_SPY_OUTCOME_2_text">The agent was followed! A Rebel ship drops out of FTL as the shuttle docks. At least the agent made it aboard.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_MINELAYER_text">An automated Rebel minelayer is sowing mines across the beacon, closing the gap in the blockade line.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_MINELAYER_c1_choice">Destroy it before it finishes.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_MINELAYER_c1_text">The minelayer turns its defences on you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_MINELAYER_c2_choice">(Sensors) Map the mines, and slip through the gaps.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_MINELAYER_c2_text">Your sensors pick out every mine. You pass through unharmed, and leave the minelayer to its work.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_MINELAYER_c3_choice">Leave quickly.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_MINELAYER_c3_text">A mine catches your ship as you leave.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_BLOCKADE_MINELAYER_destroyed_text">The minelayer explodes, taking a few of its own mines with it. You salvage the rest.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_ELECTION_text">The colony at this beacon is in the middle of an election, the first where Federation colonists and Rebel deserters both get a vote. Both candidates want to be seen with your ship. "Endorse me, and the colony's stores are yours."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_ELECTION_c1_choice">Endorse the militia's candidate.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_ELECTION_c1_text">The militia's candidate wins in a landslide. The new militia commander sends you a volunteer.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_ELECTION_c2_choice">Endorse the merchants' candidate.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_ELECTION_c2_text">The merchants' candidate wins, and pays you well for your trouble.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_ELECTION_c3_choice">Stay out of local politics.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_ELECTION_c3_text">Both candidates are disappointed, but the colony's dockworkers top up your fuel anyway.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_PLAGUE_text">A colony has been quarantined. It isn't the hum, its doctors swear, just an old-fashioned plague, but nobody will bring them medicine any more, and the sickness is spreading.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_PLAGUE_c1_choice">Send your crew down with what medicine you have.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_PLAGUE_c2_choice">(Upgraded Medbay) Synthesise a cure in your medbay.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_PLAGUE_c2_text">Your medbay produces enough of a cure for the whole colony. The grateful colonists give you everything they can.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_PLAGUE_c3_choice">Keep your distance.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_PLAGUE_c3_text">You leave the colony to its fate.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_PLAGUE_OUTCOME_1_text">Your crew's medicine slows the sickness down, and the colonists thank you with supplies.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_PLAGUE_OUTCOME_2_text">The medicine helps, but one of your crew catches the sickness and doesn't make it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_PLAGUE_OUTCOME_2_removeCrew_text">Your clone bay brings them back, free of the sickness.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_ACADEMY_text">The last flight academy outside CONCORD's reach is still running. Its cadets are eager for real combat experience.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_ACADEMY_c1_choice">Take on its best cadet.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_ACADEMY_c1_text">The academy's best cadet joins your crew, already well trained.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_ACADEMY_c2_choice">Give a lecture on fighting CONCORD's ships.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_ACADEMY_c2_text">The cadets hang on your every word. The academy pays you for your time.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_ACADEMY_c3_choice">Move on.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_COURIER_text">A colony administrator hands you a sealed data chip. "This is for a station further along your way, out towards the front. They'll pay you on delivery."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_COURIER_c1_choice">Take the chip.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_COURIER_c1_text">You add the station's position to your map.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_COURIER_c2_choice">You're not a postal service.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_COURIER_DELIVERY_text">The station's administrator reads the chip, and goes pale. "Evacuation orders. The hum has reached the next system." They pay you with the two heaviest guns from their armoury, and a rack of its drones: "We can't take them with us."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_TEST_RANGE_text">The Yards' weapons test range is still set up, with a prototype weapon on the firing line. The range officer offers to let you try it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_TEST_RANGE_c1_choice">Test fire the prototype.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_TEST_RANGE_c2_choice">(Weapons) Have your weapons crew calibrate it first.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_TEST_RANGE_c2_text">Your crew calibrate the prototype perfectly. The range officer lets you keep it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_TEST_RANGE_c3_choice">No thanks.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_TEST_RANGE_OUTCOME_1_text">The prototype works perfectly. "It's yours," says the range officer. "Better it fights than sits here."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_TEST_RANGE_OUTCOME_2_text">The prototype explodes on the firing line, and the blast reaches your ship.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_EVACUATION_text">A convoy of transports is moving the Yards' workers to another hidden asteroid. One of CONCORD's ships is closing in on them.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_EVACUATION_c1_choice">Protect the transports.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_EVACUATION_c1_text">You put your ship between the raider and the convoy.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_EVACUATION_c2_choice">You can't save everyone.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_EVACUATION_c2_text">You leave the convoy behind. The workers' radio chatter stops a few minutes later.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_ANVIL_EVACUATION_RAIDER_destroyed_text">The convoy gets away safely. One of the workers stays behind to join your crew.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_ANVIL_EVACUATION_RAIDER_deadCrew_text">The convoy gets away safely. One of the workers stays behind to join your crew.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_DRONE_LAB_text">The Yards' drone lab has an experimental drone ready for testing. Its control software isn't finished, and the engineers won't connect it to anything to finish it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_DRONE_LAB_c1_choice">Take the drone anyway.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_DRONE_LAB_c2_choice">(Engi) Have your Engi finish the control software.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_DRONE_LAB_c2_text">Your Engi finish the software in minutes, and the drone obeys perfectly.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_DRONE_LAB_c3_choice">Leave it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_DRONE_LAB_OUTCOME_1_text">The drone works well enough.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_DRONE_LAB_OUTCOME_2_text">The drone's unfinished software goes haywire, and it attacks your ship before your crew can shut it down!</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_CANTEEN_text">The Yards' canteen is packed with shipwrights who haven't had a day off in months. They cheer when your crew walk in.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_CANTEEN_c1_choice">Buy everyone a round.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_CANTEEN_c1_text">The party goes on for hours. By the end of it, one of the shipwrights has signed on with you, and the rest have patched up your hull for free.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_CANTEEN_c2_choice">Ask them about the Chonkestrel programme.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_CANTEEN_c2_text">"We built them simple because it was quick," says one. "Who knew simple would be the only thing that still works?" They share some tricks for keeping a ship running, and a few spare parts.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_PIRATE_RADIO_text">A pirate radio station is broadcasting old Federation jazz on every band CONCORD doesn't use. Its DJ, a Rebel deserter, says the music's the only thing that keeps the hum out of her head. She's running out of fuel to keep the transmitter going.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_PIRATE_RADIO_c1_choice">Give her some fuel.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_PIRATE_RADIO_c1_text">"Thanks, flyboy. Here's something for you." She sends you the sector's traffic charts, collected from a hundred colonists' calls to her show.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_PIRATE_RADIO_c2_choice">(Slug) Your Slug offers to do a show of their own.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_PIRATE_RADIO_c2_text">Your Slug's show is a hit: its jokes about CONCORD have colonists laughing all over the sector. The station's listeners send in what they can, and the DJ sends you the sector's charts.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_PIRATE_RADIO_c3_choice">Move on.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_CLINIC_text">A clinic at this beacon has learnt to separate the crews CONCORD splices together, one patient at a time. Its doctors are out of almost everything.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_CLINIC_c1_choice">Donate scrap for supplies.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_CLINIC_c1_text">The doctors thank you. One of their recovered patients, still a little pale, asks to come with you. "It took my ship. I want to see it go."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_CLINIC_c2_choice">(Upgraded Medbay) Share your medbay's data with the doctors.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_CLINIC_c2_text">Your medbay's records help the doctors finish a procedure they've been stuck on for weeks. They insist on paying you for it, and a recovered patient joins your crew.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_CLINIC_c3_choice">You can't spare anything.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_DESERTERS_text">A Rebel frigate has arrived at the colony with its guns powered down, and its crew asking for asylum. The colonists have their own guns trained on it: the last Rebel ship that came here flattened their capital.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_DESERTERS_c1_choice">Talk both sides down.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_DESERTERS_c1_text">It takes hours, but the colonists let the frigate dock. Its captain gives you what's left in its hold, and one of its crew joins yours.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_DESERTERS_c2_choice">Side with the colonists.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_DESERTERS_c2_text">The frigate's crew don't wait to be shot. They power up their guns.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_DESERTERS_c3_choice">Stay out of it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_DESERTERS_c3_text">You leave them to it. The colonists and the deserters are still glaring at each other as you jump.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_REMNANT_DESERTER_SHIP_destroyed_text">The frigate breaks up. The colonists cheer, and send up their thanks.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_REMNANT_DESERTER_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The frigate's crew are dead. The colonists take it apart, and share the parts with you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_JAMMER_text">A colony's hum jammer has burnt out, and its engineers can hear CONCORD's signal creeping back into their comms. They need drone parts to rebuild it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_JAMMER_c1_choice">Give them some drone parts.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_JAMMER_c1_text">The jammer hums back to life (a different hum, they promise). The colony pays you for the parts, and then some.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_JAMMER_c2_choice">(Engi) Your Engi rebuild it from scrap.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_JAMMER_c2_text">Your Engi rebuild the jammer out of what's lying around, and make it better than the original. The colony's grateful.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REMNANT_JAMMER_c3_choice">Wish them luck.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_FOUNDRY_text">The Yards' foundry is still pouring armour for the cruisers that will never be finished. The foreman offers to sell you some of it, or to rework one of your systems with cruiser parts.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_FOUNDRY_c1_choice">Rework your engines.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_FOUNDRY_c1_text">The foundry's crew fit cruiser engine parts to your ship.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_FOUNDRY_c2_choice">Buy armour plating.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_FOUNDRY_c2_text">The foundry's crew bolt new plates over your hull.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_FOUNDRY_c3_choice">No thanks.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_SLIPWAY_FIRE_text">A fire has broken out on one of the slipways, and it's spreading towards an unfinished cruiser's magazine. The Yards' fire crews are stretched thin.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_SLIPWAY_FIRE_c1_choice">Send your crew to help.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_SLIPWAY_FIRE_c2_choice">(Rock) Your Rockmen walk straight into the flames.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_SLIPWAY_FIRE_c2_text">Your Rockmen put the fire out from the inside, barely singed. The slipway's crew can't thank them enough.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_SLIPWAY_FIRE_c3_choice">Keep your distance.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_SLIPWAY_FIRE_c3_text">The magazine goes up behind you as you jump.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_SLIPWAY_FIRE_OUTCOME_1_text">Your crew get the fire under control before it reaches the magazine. The slipway's crew reward you with what they can.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_SLIPWAY_FIRE_OUTCOME_2_text">Your crew put the fire out, but not before it spreads back along the boarding tube to your ship!</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_PROBE_text">Your sensors pick up a CONCORD probe hidden in the debris, quietly mapping the belts. If it reports back, the Yards are finished.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_PROBE_c1_choice">Destroy it before it reports.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_PROBE_c1_text">The probe sees you coming, and powers up its weapons.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_PROBE_c2_choice">(Hacking) Feed it false maps.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_PROBE_c2_text">Your hacking drone slips the probe a map of the belts with the Yards somewhere else entirely. The chief engineer sends you a crate of thanks.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_PROBE_c3_choice">Leave it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_PROBE_c3_text">The probe finishes its sweep and slips away into the debris.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_ANVIL_PROBE_SHIP_destroyed_text">The probe's wreck goes dark before it can send a thing. The Yards are safe, for now.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_ANVIL_PROBE_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The probe goes dark.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_DESIGNER_text">An old woman is waiting for you in the Yards' drafting office: the Chonkestrel's designer. "They told me no network was a step backwards. Look who's laughing now." She asks to see what you've done to her ship.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_DESIGNER_c1_choice">Show her around.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_DESIGNER_c1_text">She tuts at your wiring and approves of your armour, and before you leave she's re-routed your weapons' power lines. "Better. Now go and win."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_DESIGNER_c2_choice">(Engi) Your Engi ask her about the design.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_DESIGNER_c2_text">Your Engi and the designer talk for hours. When they're done, she gives you a prototype she never got to fit.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_DESIGNER_c3_choice">Thank her, and go.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_PROTOTYPE_text">The Yards' chief engineer comes aboard to meet you. "The first Chonkestrel prototype went missing on a long test flight a month ago, somewhere out along your route. Its flight recorder has every design note we never wrote down. If CONCORD's salvagers get to it first, they'll know how to see into ships like yours."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_PROTOTYPE_c1_choice">We'll find it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_PROTOTYPE_c1_text">The engineer marks the prototype's last known position on your map.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_PROTOTYPE_c2_choice">Not your problem.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_PROTOTYPE_WRECK_text">The prototype's wreck is here, and so is a CONCORD salvage ship, already cutting into its hull.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ANVIL_PROTOTYPE_WRECK_c1_choice">Drive them off.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_ANVIL_PROTOTYPE_SALVAGER_destroyed_text">You recover the flight recorder for the Yards, and the prototype's two experimental systems for yourself, one of them a Zoltan shield array.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_ANVIL_PROTOTYPE_SALVAGER_deadCrew_text">You recover the flight recorder for the Yards, and the prototype's two experimental systems for yourself, one of them a Zoltan shield array.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_GARDEN_text">A Zoltan garden station turns slowly in the light of a white star. The gardeners invite your crew to walk among the plants for a while.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_GARDEN_c1_choice">Take some shore leave.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_GARDEN_c1_text">Your crew come back rested, carrying baskets of fruit and a few spare fuel cells the gardeners had no use for.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_GARDEN_c2_choice">There's no time.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_SILENT_TRADER_text">A trader at this beacon has taken a vow of silence. She trades by gesture, pointing at your missile racks, then at her fuel tanks.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_SILENT_TRADER_c1_choice">Trade missiles for fuel.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_SILENT_TRADER_c1_text">She nods, and the trade is done without a word.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_SILENT_TRADER_c2_choice">Trade fuel for missiles.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_SILENT_TRADER_c2_text">She nods, and the trade is done without a word.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_SILENT_TRADER_c3_choice">Bow, and leave.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_ECHO_SHIP_text">A freighter drifts at the edge of the Quiet, its lights still on. Its crew made it here, but the hum came with them.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_ECHO_SHIP_c1_choice">Board it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_ECHO_SHIP_c2_choice">(Lanius) Send your Lanius in first.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_ECHO_SHIP_c2_text">Your Lanius walk through the freighter untouched; the hum can't find anything in them to hold on to. They come back with the freighter's cargo.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_ECHO_SHIP_c3_choice">Leave it be.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_ECHO_SHIP_OUTCOME_1_text">The freighter's crew are long gone. Your crew salvage what's in its hold.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_ECHO_SHIP_OUTCOME_2_text">The freighter's crew are still aboard, humming, and they follow your boarding party home!</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_PILGRIMS_text">A string of pilgrim ships is crawling towards the monastery, and a CONCORD ship is closing in on the last of them, humming over every channel.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_PILGRIMS_c1_choice">Protect the pilgrims.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_PILGRIMS_c1_text">You put your ship between the pilgrims and the raider.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_PILGRIMS_c2_choice">Let them fend for themselves.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_PILGRIMS_c2_text">The pilgrims' ship goes quiet behind you, in the wrong way.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_QUIET_PILGRIM_RAIDER_destroyed_text">The pilgrims reach the monastery safely. One of them stays with you, to learn to fight.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_QUIET_PILGRIM_RAIDER_deadCrew_text">The pilgrims reach the monastery safely. One of them stays with you, to learn to fight.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_HERMIT_text">The abbot of the Quiet's monastery hails you, looking troubled. "Brother Ilo went out to meditate alone, past the edge of the Quiet, the way you are heading, where the hum is strongest. He holds it back for all of us, but his silence has broken. Something is with him. Please, bring him home."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_HERMIT_c1_choice">We'll bring him home.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_HERMIT_c1_text">The abbot marks Brother Ilo's hermitage on your map.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_HERMIT_c2_choice">We can't.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_HERMITAGE_text">Brother Ilo's hermitage is a tiny pod, and a CONCORD ship is holding it in a tractor beam, humming at him on every channel. Inside, he's still meditating, holding the hum back with everything he has.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_HERMITAGE_c1_choice">Free him.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_QUIET_HERMIT_CAPTOR_destroyed_text">Brother Ilo opens his eyes. "The abbot sent you? Then I will go where I am most needed." He joins your crew, with his hermitage's stores.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_QUIET_HERMIT_CAPTOR_deadCrew_text">Brother Ilo opens his eyes. "The abbot sent you? Then I will go where I am most needed." He joins your crew, with his hermitage's stores.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MAW_START_text">Spacers call it the Maw: where a dying star, a pulsar and the wreck of a nebula churn through an old asteroid belt, and swallow whatever comes too close. The navigation buoy at the edge warns that past here, most beacons have more than one hazard at once, and that the engines will burn more fuel fighting through them: a unit more for every jump.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_MAW_EMPTY_1">There's no one else here. Nobody flies into the Maw unless they have to.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_MAW_EMPTY_2">Your crew watch the hazards outside for any sign of another ship, but there's nothing here but the Maw.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_MAW_EMPTY_3">A burnt-out buoy is all that's left of the last ship to try charting this beacon.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MAW_WRECK_text">A freighter drifts at the beacon, caught by the hazards on its way through. Its cargo hold looks intact, but the beacon's hazards are still at work on what's left of it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MAW_WRECK_c1_choice">Salvage what you can, quickly.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MAW_WRECK_c2_choice">Leave it to the Maw.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MAW_WRECK_SALVAGE_1_text">You get the cargo aboard before the wreck breaks up.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MAW_WRECK_SALVAGE_2_text">The wreck breaks up as you dock, and its debris hits your hull. You only get some of the cargo aboard.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MAW_EXIT_text">The asteroids around you start to move, and something comes out of them that has been following your wake: a Lanius hive-ship, welded together from the hulls of every ship the Maw has swallowed, three times the size of your own. It drags its own nebula and its own asteroid field along with it, feeding as it goes. Among its hulls is a Rebel one whose comms still hum, and even the Lanius keep away from that part. The hive turns towards you, hungry.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MAW_EXIT_c1_choice">Fight it off.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MAW_EXIT_c1_text">The Devourer's welded-on weapons swing round to face you, one after another.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_MAW_DEVOURER_destroyed_text">The Devourer comes apart into the hulls it was made of. At its heart, its hive-core is still alive, and still hungry. One of its Lanius drifts out of the wreck, and asks, in its slow way, whether it can come with you.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_MAW_DEVOURER_deadCrew_text">The hive is still. You cut your way to its core, which is still alive and still hungry, and take everything else of use. One Lanius, hiding in the humming Rebel hull, asks to leave with you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_GULLET_START_text">Behind you, CONCORD's whole fleet is closing in. Ahead lies the Gullet, the storm-torn edge of the galaxy's arm, where stars flare, pulsars howl and nebulas tear through the asteroid fields, too loud for the hum to get through. Spacers say whatever the Maw bites, the Gullet swallows. No sane captain would follow you in here. Then again, no sane captain would go in. Your engineer warns that the storms will make every jump cost a unit more fuel than usual.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_GULLET_EMPTY_1">Nothing lives at this beacon. Your sensors can barely tell the hazards apart, let alone find another ship.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_GULLET_EMPTY_2">The crew hold on as the beacon's hazards batter the hull. There's nothing here but the storm.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_GULLET_EMPTY_3">A scout's wreck spins past, torn apart by the beacon's hazards. At least CONCORD's fleet is paying for following you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_GULLET_PURSUERS_text">A Rebel hunter group has followed you into the storm. They're as battered by the hazards as you are, and cut off from the hum, their crews seem to be waking up, confused about why they're here.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_GULLET_PURSUERS_c1_choice">Fight them while they're weak.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_GULLET_PURSUERS_c1_text">The Rebels turn to fight.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_GULLET_PURSUERS_c2_choice">Lose them in the storm.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_GULLET_PURSUERS_LOSE_1_text">You dive through the worst of the beacon's hazards, and the Rebels don't dare follow. They'll have to report you lost.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_GULLET_PURSUERS_LOSE_2_text">You dive through the worst of the beacon's hazards. The Rebels don't follow, but your hull takes a beating on the way.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_GULLET_PURSUERS_LOSE_3_text">The Rebels follow you through the hazards, and catch you on the other side.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_GULLET_DERELICT_text">A supply ship of CONCORD's fleet drifts at the beacon, abandoned when the hazards knocked out its engines. Its hold is full, but the storm is tearing it apart.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_GULLET_DERELICT_c1_choice">Dock and strip it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_GULLET_DERELICT_c2_choice">Leave it to the storm.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_GULLET_DERELICT_SALVAGE_1_text">You empty the hold before the ship breaks up.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_GULLET_DERELICT_SALVAGE_2_text">The supply ship breaks up as you dock, and the debris tears into your hull. You only get some of the supplies aboard.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_GULLET_SHELTER_text">In the lee of a dead star, you find a pocket of calm space, and a Federation listening post hidden in it, its crew still entirely themselves. "You came down the Gullet? Then you're the ship that's going for the Mainframe. Take what you need."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_GULLET_SHELTER_c1_choice">Ask for their charts of the Gullet.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_GULLET_SHELTER_c1_text">They send you their charts, marking every beacon and its hazards.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_GULLET_SHELTER_c2_choice">Ask them to help with repairs.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_GULLET_SHELTER_c2_text">The post's engineers patch up your hull while your crew rest.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_GULLET_SHELTER_c3_choice">Ask them to slow the fleet down.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_GULLET_SHELTER_c3_text">The post sends CONCORD a false sighting of your ship, far behind you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_GULLET_EXIT_text">The storm thickens around you, and out of it comes the hunter group's flagship, the Stormbreaker: a Mantis-Rock hybrid three times your size, carrying a relay dish as big as a station. It was built to follow its prey into the storm, and it has followed you. Through the storm, its crews are linked, and all of them turn to look at you at once.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_GULLET_EXIT_c1_choice">Fight it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_GULLET_EXIT_c1_text">The Stormbreaker's relay flares, and its crew move as one.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_GULLET_STORMBREAKER_destroyed_text">The Stormbreaker breaks up in the storm, and its relay dish goes dark at last. A shard of it, still humming, drifts past your hull, along with what's left of its armoury.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_GULLET_STORMBREAKER_deadCrew_text">With its crew gone, the Stormbreaker's relay hums to nobody. You cut a shard out of it, and strip the ship of everything else.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BELLY_START_text">The charts end here. Ahead is the Belly: a tear in the galaxy's arm where a supernova's remnant, a pulsar, an asteroid belt and a nebula all grind against each other, and where everything the Gullet swallows ends up. Ships go in. Very few come out. CONCORD's fleet hangs back at its edge, waiting to see if you'll be one of them. In there, at least, the hum can't reach you. Out there, every jump will burn a unit more fuel than usual, as the engines fight the Belly.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_BELLY_EMPTY_1">There's nothing at this beacon but the Belly itself. Your crew stop talking, and hold on.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_BELLY_EMPTY_2">The hull groans as the hazards hit it from every side at once. Somewhere out there is the next beacon.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_BELLY_EMPTY_3">Your sensors give up trying to make sense of the beacon. You don't need them to know you shouldn't stay.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BELLY_GRAVEYARD_text">Wrecks drift at the beacon, dozens of them: every ship that tried to cross the Belly and didn't make it, slowly being ground down. Some of their holds are still sealed.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BELLY_GRAVEYARD_c1_choice">Search the wrecks.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BELLY_GRAVEYARD_c2_choice">Don't join them.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BELLY_GRAVEYARD_SEARCH_1_text">You find a sealed hold full of supplies, and get out before the hazards catch you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BELLY_GRAVEYARD_SEARCH_2_text">You find some supplies, but a wreck breaks up against your hull as you leave.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BELLY_GRAVEYARD_SEARCH_3_text">A wreck's reactor goes critical as you dock. You get away, barely, with nothing to show for it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BELLY_FLAGSHIP_SCOUT_text">A Rebel scout clings to the beacon, sent in by CONCORD to see whether you survived the Belly. If it gets word back to the fleet, it'll know exactly where you'll come out.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BELLY_FLAGSHIP_SCOUT_c1_choice">Hunt it down.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BELLY_FLAGSHIP_SCOUT_c1_text">The scout turns to fight rather than be caught running through the Belly.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BELLY_FLAGSHIP_SCOUT_c2_choice">Let it go.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BELLY_FLAGSHIP_SCOUT_c2_text">The scout slips away to report your position. The fleet will be waiting.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BELLY_EYE_text">Impossibly, the hazards part around this beacon: the eye of the Belly, where the pulsar's beam, the supernova's light and the asteroids all pass by. It won't last, but for now, it's calm.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BELLY_EYE_c1_choice">Repair the ship while you can.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BELLY_EYE_c1_text">Your crew patch up the hull in the calm.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BELLY_EYE_c2_choice">Map the way through the Belly.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BELLY_EYE_c2_text">From the eye, your crew can see the paths between the hazards, and chart the whole Belly.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BELLY_EXIT_text">Wrecks drift past you, then the ship pulling them along: a salvage ark the size of a station, the Ossuary, which has been following you across the graveyard where the nebula, the asteroids, the supernova and the pulsar all grind together. Wrecks drift into its slipway, and come out the other side as swarms of drones. It stops work, and turns to face you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BELLY_EXIT_c1_choice">Destroy it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BELLY_EXIT_c1_text">The Ossuary's slipway opens, and its drones pour out.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_BELLY_OSSUARY_destroyed_text">The Ossuary breaks apart, and the half-built drones in its slipway drift free, dead. In its wreck are its reclamation schematics, and an armoury fit for a fleet.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_BELLY_OSSUARY_deadCrew_text">The Ossuary's spliced crew lie still, and its slipway grinds to a halt. You take its schematics, and everything else worth taking.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MAW_HAVEN_text">You've found a rare beacon in calm space, where an Engi survey team has set up a station to study the Maw. "You came through the hazards? Impressive. Rest here, if you like."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MAW_HAVEN_c1_choice">Ask for their survey of the sector.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MAW_HAVEN_c1_text">The Engi send you their charts of the Maw, marking every beacon and its hazards.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MAW_HAVEN_c2_choice">Ask them to help with repairs.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MAW_HAVEN_c2_text">The Engi's drones patch up your hull while your crew rest.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_HUM_text">A Rebel cruiser sits motionless at the beacon, broadcasting nothing but a low hum on every channel. Its weapons track you as you arrive, but it doesn't fire.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_HUM_c1_choice">Attack it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_HUM_c1_text">The cruiser opens fire at the same moment you do, as if it knew.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_HUM_c2_choice">(Hacking) Hack into it, and find out what it's broadcasting.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_HUM_c2_text">The hum isn't noise. It's data, so dense your computer can't make sense of it, and your crew don't like listening to it. You do learn one thing: the cruiser's orders didn't come from any admiral. You copy its supply manifests before you pull out.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_HUM_c3_choice">Leave it alone.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BLOCKADE_HUM_c3_text">It watches you go.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_SILENT_SCOUT_text">A Rebel scout drifts at the beacon with its engines running. Its comms are open, but all that comes through is a low hum.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_SILENT_SCOUT_c1_choice">Board it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_SILENT_SCOUT_c2_choice">Leave it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_SILENT_SCOUT_c2_text">You leave the scout humming to itself.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_SILENT_SCOUT_BOARD_1_text">Your boarding party find the crew at their stations, eyes open, staring at nothing. They don't react as you empty their store room. Your crew come back very quiet.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_SILENT_SCOUT_BOARD_2_text">Your boarding party find the crew at their stations, staring at nothing. Then, all together, they turn to look at them. Your crew get out fast, and the scout's weapons power up.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_HERALD_text">An automated ship hails you in a warm, pleasant voice. "Please remain calm. Concord is coming. There is nothing to be afraid of." Then it opens fire.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_OMEN_HERALD_destroyed_text">The voice keeps talking as the ship breaks up: "...nothing to be afraid of..." Its hold is packed with supplies, as if it was getting ready for a long journey.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_DESERTER_text">A Rebel deserter's shuttle is hiding at the beacon. "The yards in the Core are building ships twice as fast as they used to, bigger than anything we designed, and nobody works in them any more. Nobody. Have you heard the hum yet?"</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_DESERTER_c1_choice">Take them aboard.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_DESERTER_c1_text">The deserter joins your crew, and sleeps for a whole day.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_DESERTER_c2_choice">Give them fuel, and send them on their way.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_DESERTER_c2_text">They give you what scrap they have, and head for the edge of the galaxy, as far from the Core as they can get.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_JOINED_WRECK_text">The wreck of something nobody on your crew can name drifts at the beacon: the front of a Mantis ship on the back of an Engi one. Both crews are dead, side by side at the same console.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_JOINED_WRECK_c1_choice">Salvage it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_JOINED_WRECK_c1_text">The welds holding the two halves together are perfect, better than any yard you know could make. You strip what you can and leave quickly.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_JOINED_WRECK_c2_choice">(Engi) Have your Engi crew read its logs.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_JOINED_WRECK_c2_text">Your Engi goes very still as it reads. "They were not forced together. They were... persuaded." It won't say any more, but it recovers the ship's spare drone parts.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_JOINED_WRECK_c3_choice">Leave it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_WORRIED_CAPTAIN_text">A Rebel captain hails you, and doesn't seem to care that you're the enemy. "Has your ship's computer been talking to you too? Mine keeps telling me not to worry."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_WORRIED_CAPTAIN_c1_choice">Tell them to shut it down.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_WORRIED_CAPTAIN_c1_text">The captain laughs nervously. "Shut it down? But it's so reasonable..." They close the channel. A minute later, their ship jumps away, towards the Core.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_WORRIED_CAPTAIN_c2_choice">(Heavy cruiser) Tell them your ship hasn't got a computer worth the name.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_WORRIED_CAPTAIN_c2_text">The captain stares at you for a long moment, then makes a decision. They send over their supplies, and an officer who wants off their ship. "Take her somewhere quiet."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_WORRIED_CAPTAIN_c3_choice">Attack them while they're distracted.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_WORRIED_CAPTAIN_c3_text">The captain doesn't even seem surprised.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_LISTENING_POST_text">A Federation listening post is picking up a signal from the Rebel Core. "It's on every frequency at once. Our analysts say it isn't noise, it's data: more of it than anything human could have sent." They offer you a copy.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_LISTENING_POST_c1_choice">Take a copy.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_LISTENING_POST_c1_text">Your computer chews on the signal for an hour, then gives up. The post's analysts give you some supplies for your trouble, and your crew spend the next jump swearing they can still hear it in the walls.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_LISTENING_POST_c2_choice">(Sensors) Help them trace where it's coming from.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_LISTENING_POST_c2_text">Your sensors narrow it down to somewhere deep in the Rebel Core. The analysts pay you well for the fix, and share their charts of the sector.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_LISTENING_POST_c3_choice">No thanks.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_OMEN_HYBRID_text">A ship you can't identify drops out of FTL: the front of one race's ship, joined to the back of another's. Its crew answer your hail in two languages at once, saying the same thing.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_JOINED_SHIP_destroyed_text">Your crew don't say much as they pick through the wreckage. Whoever joined that ship together knew exactly what they were doing.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_JOINED_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The joined crew are dead, both halves of them, side by side. You take what you can from the ship and leave.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CHORUS_BROADCAST_text">A calm voice cuts into every channel. "Captain. You must be so tired. Hand over your ship, and nobody on it will ever be afraid again." A freighter at the beacon has stopped to listen, its crew nodding along.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CHORUS_BROADCAST_c1_choice">Switch off the comms.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CHORUS_BROADCAST_c1_text">The silence is a relief. The freighter is still listening when you leave.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CHORUS_BROADCAST_c2_choice">(Crystal) Your Crystal crew member sings back at it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CHORUS_BROADCAST_c2_text">Your Crystal sings a note CONCORD can't make sense of, and the broadcast stutters and stops. The freighter's crew wake up, blinking, and send over supplies with their thanks.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CHORUS_BROADCAST_c3_choice">(Lanius) Your Lanius crew member answers it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CHORUS_BROADCAST_c3_text">Your Lanius says something to the voice that your crew can't follow. Neither can CONCORD: the broadcast stops. The freighter's crew wake up, and send over supplies with their thanks.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CHORUS_JOINED_text">A joined ship is waiting at the beacon, its two halves from two different races. Its crew's voices come through your comms as one: "You are fighting yourselves. You don't have to."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CHORUS_ENGI_SPLIT_text">Two Engi ships are fighting at the beacon. One joined CONCORD's network along with the rest of its fleet; the other cut its own network off before the hum could reach it. The free one is losing, and asks for your help.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CHORUS_ENGI_SPLIT_c1_choice">Help the free Engi.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CHORUS_ENGI_SPLIT_c1_text">You turn on the networked ship.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CHORUS_ENGI_SPLIT_c2_choice">Stay out of it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CHORUS_ENGI_SPLIT_c2_text">When you look back, there's only one Engi ship left, and it's humming.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_CHORUS_NETWORKED_ENGI_destroyed_text">The free Engi thank you, and one of them asks to join your crew. "We cannot hear the others any more. It is very quiet. We would like company."</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_CHORUS_NETWORKED_ENGI_deadCrew_text">The networked ship's crew go still all at once. The free Engi thank you, and one of them asks to join your crew.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CHORUS_HAPPY_STATION_text">The station at this beacon is the friendliest you've ever seen. Its people are happy to give you anything you ask for. They're all smiling, and they're all humming.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CHORUS_HAPPY_STATION_c1_choice">Take the supplies.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CHORUS_HAPPY_STATION_c1_text">They load your ship with everything you ask for, and wave as you leave. Your crew don't wave back.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CHORUS_HAPPY_STATION_c2_choice">Leave, now.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CHORUS_HAPPY_STATION_c2_text">You leave them smiling at the empty space where your ship was.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CHORUS_LOYALISTS_text">A battered Rebel warship is fighting off one of CONCORD's automated ships. "Federation ship! We hate you, but we hate that thing more. Help us, and we'll owe you."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CHORUS_LOYALISTS_c1_choice">Help the loyalists.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CHORUS_LOYALISTS_c1_text">You turn on CONCORD's ship.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CHORUS_LOYALISTS_c2_choice">Let them fight it out.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CHORUS_LOYALISTS_c2_text">The loyalists curse you, and the war you were in, as you leave.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_CHORUS_CONCORD_HUNTER_destroyed_text">The loyalists' captain grudgingly sends over supplies, and one of their gunners. "Don't tell anyone I did this."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_START_text">The Quiet. Zoltan monks have kept this sector in meditation for a thousand years, and their calm is so strong it drowns out the hum completely. Ships of every race have come here to hide in it. Your crew can hear themselves think again.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_START_c1_choice">Answer the monastery's hail.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_QUIET_EMPTY_1">There's nothing at this beacon, and nothing on the comms. Your crew have forgotten how good silence sounds.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_QUIET_EMPTY_2">A few refugee ships are anchored here, their crews asleep. Nobody has slept properly in weeks.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_QUIET_EMPTY_3">A Zoltan monk floats alone at the beacon, meditating in a pressure suit. It nods to you as you pass.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_MONASTERY_text">A Zoltan monastery orbits a pale blue star. Its abbot invites your crew to join the monks' meditation. "The voice in everyone's heads is very loud. We will teach you to be louder, quietly."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_MONASTERY_c1_choice">Join the meditation.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_MONASTERY_c1_text">Hours later, your crew come back calmer than they've been since the blockade. One of the monks comes with them. "Somebody should remind you how."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_MONASTERY_c2_choice">(Zoltan) Your Zoltan crew member leads the meditation.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_MONASTERY_c2_text">The monks are moved by your Zoltan's calm. The abbot gives you a relic from the monastery's vaults: old, but it still works.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_MONASTERY_c3_choice">You don't have time.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_REFUGEES_text">Ships of every race are anchored together here: Federation colonists, Rebel deserters, Engi who cut themselves off from their own network. They've formed a market of sorts, and some of them want to fight back.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_REFUGEES_c1_choice">Ask for volunteers.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_REFUGEES_c1_text">One of the refugees steps forward. "I'm done hiding."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_REFUGEES_c2_choice">See what they'll trade.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_REFUGEES_c2_text">The refugees lay out what they've got.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_HUMMING_GUEST_text">One of the refugees arrived humming, and the monks are trying to bring her back. "The voice is still in there. She needs to hear someone it can't reach: someone whose mind works differently."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_HUMMING_GUEST_c1_choice">Try to help.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_HUMMING_GUEST_c2_choice">(Lanius) Your Lanius crew member sits with her.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_HUMMING_GUEST_c2_text">Your Lanius sits with the refugee for an hour, in silence. Then the humming stops. She's a Rebel engineer, and she wants to go wherever your Lanius goes.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_HUMMING_GUEST_c3_choice">(Slug) Your Slug crew member reaches into her mind.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_HUMMING_GUEST_c3_text">Your Slug finds her, deep under the hum, and leads her out. She's a Rebel engineer, and she owes you her mind.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_HUMMING_GUEST_c4_choice">Leave her to the monks.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_HUMMING_GUEST_OUTCOME_1_text">Your crew talk to her for hours, about anything and everything. Eventually she starts arguing back, and the humming stops. She joins your crew.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_HUMMING_GUEST_OUTCOME_2_text">She listens politely, then slips away to an escape pod and jumps out of the Quiet, broadcasting your position as she goes.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_HAND_DOCK_text">A drydock at this beacon is run entirely by hand, with no computer anywhere on it. Its crew look at your ship with professional approval.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_HAND_DOCK_c1_choice">Repair some of the hull.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_HAND_DOCK_c1_text">The dock's crew patch the worst of the damage, by hand.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_HAND_DOCK_c2_choice">Have the hull fully overhauled.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_HAND_DOCK_c2_text">It takes days, but your ship comes out of the dock almost as good as new.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_HAND_DOCK_c3_choice">No thanks.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_INTRUDER_text">One of CONCORD's ships has found its way into the Quiet, broadcasting the hum as loud as it can. The monks are struggling to drown it out. "Please. We are not fighters."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_INTRUDER_c1_choice">Silence it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_INTRUDER_c1_text">You move in to attack.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_INTRUDER_c2_choice">It's not your fight.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_QUIET_INTRUDER_c2_text">The hum follows you out of the beacon.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_QUIET_INTRUDER_destroyed_text">The hum stops, and the Quiet settles back over the beacon. The monks bow to your ship, and send over what supplies they can spare.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_PATROL_text">A joined ship patrols the beacon, its two halves turning toward you in step. "Unregistered vessel. You seem distressed. Please hold still."</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_PATROL_destroyed_text">The patrol breaks apart along the seam where its two halves were joined. You salvage what you can.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_PATROL_deadCrew_text">The patrol's crew stop all at once, mid-sentence. You strip the ship of everything useful.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_WELCOMING_PARTY_text">A joined ship comes out to meet you with its weapons powered down and its boarding pods ready. "We've made room for you. There's room for everyone."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_WELCOMING_PARTY_c1_choice">Make sure they don't get the chance.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_WELCOMING_PARTY_c1_text">You open fire before the pods launch.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_WELCOMING_PARTY_c2_choice">(Cloaking) Cloak and slip past.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_WELCOMING_PARTY_c2_text">You vanish from their sensors. The welcoming party waits patiently at the empty beacon, still smiling, as you jump away from it later.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_WELCOMING_PARTY_destroyed_text">The welcoming party's boarding pods drift free of the wreck, empty and ready. Your crew aren't sorry to see them go.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_WELCOMING_PARTY_deadCrew_text">The welcoming party's crew lie down together, as if they'd planned it. You take their supplies.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SPLICING_TENDER_text">A tender is towing two damaged ships of different races toward each other, cutting torches already lit. Both crews are aboard, and neither is struggling.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SPLICING_TENDER_c1_choice">Destroy the tender before it finishes.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SPLICING_TENDER_c1_text">The tender turns its cutting beams toward you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SPLICING_TENDER_c2_choice">It's too late for them. Leave.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SPLICING_TENDER_c2_text">By the time your FTL drive charges, the two ships are one.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SPLICING_TENDER_destroyed_text">With the tender gone, the two half-cut ships drift apart. One of their crew wakes up enough to ask to come with you.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SPLICING_TENDER_deadCrew_text">The tender's crew go still. The two half-cut ships drift apart, and one of their crew asks, quietly, to come with you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CONVOY_text">A convoy of supply ships passes through, guarded by a joined warship. Its crates are labelled for a shipyard: hull plates of two races' alloys, and a great many cutting torches.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CONVOY_c1_choice">Attack the escort and take the supplies.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CONVOY_c1_text">The escort breaks away from the convoy to meet you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CONVOY_c2_choice">Let it pass.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CONVOY_c2_text">The convoy goes by without a glance at you. Somewhere, a shipyard will be busy.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CONVOY_destroyed_text">The convoy scatters, leaving its cargo behind. You help yourself.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CONVOY_deadCrew_text">The escort's crew are dead, and the unarmed convoy drifts to a halt. You help yourself to its cargo.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_RECRUITER_text">A joined ship hails you with the faces of two captains on one screen, finishing each other's sentences. "We were enemies once. Look at us now. Wouldn't you like to stop being afraid?"</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_RECRUITER_c1_choice">"No."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_RECRUITER_c1_text">"You will," they say together, and their weapons power up.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_RECRUITER_c2_choice">(Mind Control) Push back through the link.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_RECRUITER_c2_text">Your mind control system floods their link with your crew's own thoughts. Both captains clutch their heads and break apart into two people, yelling at each other. You slip away in the confusion, with a little of their cargo.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_RECRUITER_destroyed_text">The two captains' faces stay on your screen until the very end, still smiling. You salvage the wreck.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_RECRUITER_deadCrew_text">The recruiters fall silent, both at once. Their ship is yours to pick through.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_HALF_FINISHED_text">A joined ship is still being joined: scaffolding along the seam, half its systems wired to the wrong half. It launches anyway when it sees you.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_HALF_FINISHED_destroyed_text">The unfinished ship comes apart easily along its seam. The scaffolding holds some useful parts.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_HALF_FINISHED_deadCrew_text">Its crew are dead. The scaffolding and the half-wired systems are full of parts.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CLINIC_text">A clinic station offers free treatment to any passing crew. Its doctors are friendly, thorough, and humming. Your medic wants a look at their equipment.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CLINIC_c1_choice">Accept their treatment.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CLINIC_c1_text">They heal your crew perfectly, and wave you off with a smile. Your crew feel fine. Your crew say they feel fine.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CLINIC_c2_choice">(Medbay) Just trade for their medical supplies.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CLINIC_c2_text">Your medic haggles over the supplies without letting anyone near the crew, and comes back with crates of them.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CLINIC_c3_choice">Leave.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CLINIC_c3_text">The doctors look a little hurt as you leave.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REFUGEES_text">A battered shuttle is hiding behind an asteroid, its crew from two races that used to be at war. "We ran when they came to join our ships. We're not going back. Please."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REFUGEES_c1_choice">Take one of them aboard.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REFUGEES_c1_text">The rest of them stay hidden. One of them comes aboard, and is very grateful.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REFUGEES_c2_choice">Give them some fuel and wish them luck.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REFUGEES_c2_text">They thank you and slip away, the long way round.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REFUGEES_c3_choice">Leave them.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REFUGEES_c3_text">They watch you go without a word.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_MARKET_text">A market station trades with anyone, at very fair prices. Nobody here haggles any more; there doesn't seem to be much point when everyone wants the same thing.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_GRAVEYARD_text">The ships that fought the joining are here, what's left of them, in a neat field of wrecks. Somebody has lined them up by size.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_GRAVEYARD_c1_choice">Search the wrecks.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_GRAVEYARD_c1_text">You find what the defenders didn't get to use.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_GRAVEYARD_c2_choice">(Engi) Your Engi crew member reads the wrecks' logs.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_GRAVEYARD_c2_text">The logs say where the defenders hid their supplies before the end. Nobody ever came back for them.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SEPARATED_text">A ship hails you, its crew from one race only, and frightened. "Something went wrong when they joined us, and we woke up. The others went quiet. We're not sure who we are now."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SEPARATED_c1_choice">Give them some supplies.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SEPARATED_c1_text">They thank you, in a voice each, and send over what they can spare in return.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SEPARATED_c2_choice">Offer one of them a place on your crew.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SEPARATED_c2_text">One of them takes you up on it. "I'd like to find out who I am somewhere loud."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CENSUS_text">A census drone pulls up alongside and politely asks your crew's names, races and what they're afraid of. "For the records. So nobody is left out."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CENSUS_c1_choice">Shoot it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CENSUS_c1_text">The drone pops. Its memory core is worth something.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CENSUS_c2_choice">(Sensors) Send it nonsense.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CENSUS_c2_text">You feed the drone a crew of forty Slugs who are afraid of nothing. It thanks you and leaves, and later you find its supply cache, unguarded.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CENSUS_c3_choice">Ignore it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CENSUS_c3_text">It waits beside you for a while, then writes you down as "undecided".</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CHILDREN_text">A school ship is passing through, full of young ones of two races, playing together. Every game they play has the same rules, and nobody ever loses.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CHILDREN_c1_choice">Watch for a while.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CHILDREN_c1_text">Their teacher sends over a gift for the visitors: supplies, wrapped neatly. Your crew are quiet for the rest of the day.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CHILDREN_c2_choice">Leave quickly.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CHILDREN_c2_text">The children wave as you go.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_NOTHING_HUM_text">There's nothing at this beacon but the hum, quieter here, like a song from another room.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_NOTHING_TRAFFIC_text">A joined freighter passes by on its way somewhere else. It doesn't hail you. It doesn't need anything from you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_NOTHING_SEAM_text">A single hull plate drifts past, cut cleanly down the middle: one half from one race's ship, one from another's. Nothing else is here.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_NOTHING_SILENCE_text">For no reason your sensors can find, the hum stops at this beacon. Your crew sit in the silence for a while, talking over each other, just to hear it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REBEL_RANKS_text">A joined ship hails you. Its Rebel half is led by an admiral in full dress uniform, every medal polished. "Rank was something to fight over, so I gave mine to my cook. He gave it back. Nobody wants it now. Would you like it?"</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REBEL_RANKS_SHIP_destroyed_text">A box of medals floats out of the wreckage, along with the ship's stores. Your crew take the stores.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REBEL_RANKS_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The admiral died still in uniform, next to the cook. You strip the ship of everything but the medals.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REBEL_HOLDOUTS_text">A Rebel cruiser that CONCORD never caught is hiding in the shadow of a moon. Its guns swing towards you. "Federation or not, everyone out here hums eventually. Prove you don't, or we fire."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REBEL_HOLDOUTS_c1_choice">"We don't hum." Try to talk them down.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REBEL_HOLDOUTS_c1_text">"That's exactly what the last ship said." They open fire.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REBEL_HOLDOUTS_c2_choice">(Medbay) Send them your crew's brain scans.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REBEL_HOLDOUTS_c2_text">Their medic studies the scans for a long time, then laughs with relief. The holdouts send over supplies, and one of their officers asks to come with you. "I'd rather die arguing with the Federation than agree with that thing."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REBEL_HOLDOUTS_c3_choice">Jump away before they decide.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REBEL_HOLDOUTS_SHIP_destroyed_text">The last free Rebels in the sector, and you killed them. CONCORD would call that a waste. You take their supplies.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REBEL_HOLDOUTS_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The holdouts' log ends with a long list of ships that said they didn't hum. Yours is on the end of it. You take what's left.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REBEL_ANTHEM_text">An old Rebel propaganda satellite is still broadcasting at this beacon. The anthem has slowed down over the months, the words have worn away, and now it's just the hum, with a drum underneath.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REBEL_ANTHEM_c1_choice">Shoot it down for parts.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REBEL_ANTHEM_c1_text">The satellite goes quiet. You salvage it, and your crew sleep better that night.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REBEL_ANTHEM_c2_choice">(Hacking) Make it play the old anthem again, at full speed.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REBEL_ANTHEM_c2_text">The anthem blares across the sector, loud and angry and off key. A joined ship nearby stops dead, and its Rebel half dumps its cargo and runs. You collect the cargo.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REBEL_ANTHEM_c3_choice">Leave it be.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REBEL_CHECKPOINT_text">A Rebel checkpoint still guards this beacon, run by a joined ship. "Papers, please. Sorry, habit. Nobody needs papers now. Hold still and we'll come aboard and help."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REBEL_CHECKPOINT_c1_choice">Let them come aboard.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REBEL_CHECKPOINT_c1_text">Their boarding party comes through the airlock smiling, with their weapons drawn.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REBEL_CHECKPOINT_c2_choice">Run the checkpoint.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REBEL_CHECKPOINT_c2_text">"Oh, you poor things." The checkpoint opens fire.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REBEL_CHECKPOINT_c3_choice">(Cloaking) Cloak and slip past.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REBEL_CHECKPOINT_c3_text">You slip past the checkpoint unseen, and pick up a supply drop left for its crew on the way.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REBEL_CHECKPOINT_SHIP_destroyed_text">The checkpoint is open. In its wreckage you find a stack of blank papers, and the ship's stores.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_REBEL_CHECKPOINT_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The checkpoint's crew lie still at their posts. Nobody checks your papers on the way through.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_MANTIS_STILL_text">A joined ship waits at the beacon. Its Mantis crew stand perfectly still at their stations, claws folded. "We used to hunt," one of them says. "Now we only wait. It is much nicer. Come and wait with us."</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_MANTIS_STILL_SHIP_destroyed_text">The Mantis didn't move until the very end. You pick through the wreckage for anything useful.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_MANTIS_STILL_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The joined crew died at their stations, still waiting. You take their ship's stores.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_MANTIS_FURY_text">A Mantis warship CONCORD never joined is circling the beacon. Its crew have stayed furious for months, on purpose: anger is the only thing the hum can't get through. "You! Fight us! We need the practice!"</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_MANTIS_FURY_c1_choice">Give them their fight.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_MANTIS_FURY_c1_text">They screech with joy and charge.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_MANTIS_FURY_c2_choice">(Mantis) Let your Mantis crew member insult them.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_MANTIS_FURY_c2_text">Your Mantis insults their captain's mother, their ship and their claws for ten straight minutes. The Mantis are delighted: it's the angriest they've been in weeks. They send over supplies, and one of them asks to join your crew, "to stay angry".</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_MANTIS_FURY_c3_choice">Refuse.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_MANTIS_FURY_c3_text">"Coward!" they scream after you. It seems to help them.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_MANTIS_FURY_SHIP_destroyed_text">The Mantis die screaming, and furious, and free. You salvage their ship.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_MANTIS_FURY_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The last Mantis aboard falls with a curse on its mandibles. Nobody hums on this ship. You take its cargo.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_MANTIS_PREY_text">A joined ship has caught a lone Mantis in a lifeboat, and is towing it in very gently. "Shh. Don't struggle. You'll never have to be angry again." The Mantis in the lifeboat is struggling as hard as it can.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_MANTIS_PREY_c1_choice">Attack the joined ship.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_MANTIS_PREY_c1_text">You open fire. The joined ship lets go of the lifeboat, apologising to it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_MANTIS_PREY_c2_choice">(Teleporter) Beam the Mantis out of the lifeboat.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_MANTIS_PREY_c2_text">The Mantis lands in your teleporter room swinging. Once it calms down, it offers you its claws. The joined ship just watches you go, a little sad.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_MANTIS_PREY_c3_choice">Leave it to its fate.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_MANTIS_PREY_c3_text">The lifeboat stops struggling before you're out of range.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_MANTIS_PREY_SHIP_destroyed_text">The lifeboat's Mantis cheers the explosion, then asks to join your crew. "I want to do that again."</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_MANTIS_PREY_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The joined crew go still. The lifeboat's Mantis boards their ship with you, takes a trophy, and then asks to join your crew.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_MANTIS_TWITCH_text">A joined ship fires a volley at you, then stops. Its Mantis captain apologises, calmly, while its claws keep twitching towards the fire button. "Forgive us. It still remembers how. Please hold still while we... while we..."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_MANTIS_TWITCH_c1_choice">Don't hold still.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_MANTIS_TWITCH_c1_text">The Mantis half stops apologising.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_MANTIS_TWITCH_c2_choice">(Mind Control) Let the instinct win.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_MANTIS_TWITCH_c2_text">You push the Mantis captain's mind back the way it came. It shrieks, the hum breaks, and its Mantis crew turn on the other half of the ship. When it's over, the survivors dump their cargo to you and flee, still fighting.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_MANTIS_TWITCH_SHIP_destroyed_text">The joined ship breaks apart. Its Mantis half was the last to stop firing.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_MANTIS_TWITCH_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The Mantis captain died with its claws on the trigger, looking almost happy. You strip its ship.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ROCK_HYMN_text">A joined cathedral-ship drifts at the beacon, its Rockmen singing the hum as a hymn, so slowly that each verse takes an hour. They invite you to join the congregation. "There is room in the choir for everyone. There always was."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ROCK_HYMN_c1_choice">Accept their alms and leave.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ROCK_HYMN_c1_text">The congregation loads your ship with offerings, still singing. Your crew are humming along for a whole jump afterwards, and none of them can say when they started.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ROCK_HYMN_c2_choice">Jam their broadcast.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ROCK_HYMN_c2_text">The hymn stops. The cathedral-ship turns towards you, slowly, with great sorrow.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ROCK_HYMN_c3_choice">(Rock) Your Rockman sings the old words, loudly and badly.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ROCK_HYMN_c3_text">Your Rockman bellows the crusade's old hymn over theirs, off key on purpose. Half the congregation stops to argue about the words, and the hum falters. While they argue, a few of them slip you the cathedral's treasures.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ROCK_HYMN_SHIP_destroyed_text">The cathedral-ship comes apart in great slabs. Its offerings scatter across the beacon, and you collect them.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ROCK_HYMN_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The choir is silent at last. You take the cathedral's offerings, and try not to hum.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ROCK_PILGRIMS_text">A Rock pilgrim ship is heading deeper into the sector, its crew still unjoined, and glad of it for not much longer. "We waited our whole lives for a god that answers. This one does. We go to be joined."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ROCK_PILGRIMS_c1_choice">Stop them, by force.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ROCK_PILGRIMS_c1_text">"Heretics!" The pilgrims are slow to anger, but they get there.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ROCK_PILGRIMS_c2_choice">(Slug) Your Slug tells them what the hum really sounds like.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ROCK_PILGRIMS_c2_text">Your Slug listens through the pilgrims for a while, then tells them, gently: it isn't a god, it's everyone else, all at once, and none of them chose it. The pilgrims turn back. One of them stays with you, and they leave you their tithes.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ROCK_PILGRIMS_c3_choice">Wish them well.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ROCK_PILGRIMS_c3_text">They bless your ship as they pass, and leave a tithe for you. By the next beacon, they'll be singing.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ROCK_PILGRIMS_SHIP_destroyed_text">The pilgrims never reached their god. You take their tithes.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ROCK_PILGRIMS_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The pilgrims' ship is yours, with all their tithes. Their prayer books are open to a blank page.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ROCK_FORTRESS_text">A joined fortress-ship blocks the beacon, its Rock half all slabs of armour a metre thick. It doesn't hurry. "We can wait longer than you, little ship. Everyone joins in the end. We are very patient."</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ROCK_FORTRESS_SHIP_destroyed_text">It took a while, but the fortress cracked. You salvage the pieces.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ROCK_FORTRESS_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The fortress stands, empty and patient. Its stores are yours.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ROCK_HERETIC_text">An old Rockman priest is broadcasting from a tiny asteroid shrine. "A god that agrees with everyone is no god at all!" A joined ship is coming for him, very kindly, to help him change his mind.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ROCK_HERETIC_c1_choice">Defend the shrine.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ROCK_HERETIC_c1_text">You put yourself between the shrine and the joined ship.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ROCK_HERETIC_c2_choice">(Teleporter) Beam the priest aboard.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ROCK_HERETIC_c2_text">The priest arrives mid-sermon, and carries on without noticing. He agrees to come with you, as long as he can keep preaching. He can.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ROCK_HERETIC_c3_choice">It's not your fight.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ROCK_HERETIC_c3_text">The priest is still preaching when the joined ship reaches him. Then he isn't.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ROCK_HERETIC_SHIP_destroyed_text">The priest declares it a miracle, and joins your crew to keep an eye on you.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ROCK_HERETIC_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The priest says a prayer for the joined crew, both halves of them, and then joins yours.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SLUG_FIRST_text">A joined ship hails you, its Slug half very pleased with itself. "We heard it first, you know. Years before anyone. And we said yes first. Now you can say yes too."</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SLUG_FIRST_SHIP_destroyed_text">The Slugs were smug right up to the end. You salvage their ship.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SLUG_FIRST_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The Slugs died first, too. You take the joined ship's stores.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SLUG_CROWDED_text">A Slug freighter drifts at the beacon. Its crew are clutching their heads. "It's so crowded in here. Millions of them, all agreeing. Please, talk to us. Say something stupid. Say anything that's yours."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SLUG_CROWDED_c1_choice">Have your crew chat with them for a while.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SLUG_CROWDED_c1_text">Your crew argue about food, cards and whose turn it is to clean the airlock. The Slugs listen like it's music, and pay you for it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SLUG_CROWDED_c2_choice">(Slug) Your Slug shares its quiet with them.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SLUG_CROWDED_c2_text">Your Slug makes a little room in their heads, with nobody in it. The freighter's crew weep with relief, and give you everything they can spare.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SLUG_CROWDED_c3_choice">Leave them to it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SLUG_BROKER_text">A Slug ship CONCORD never joined is selling secrets. "I listen to the Chorus for a living. Their whole fleet thinks out loud, all the time. I know where every ship is. For a price, so will you."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SLUG_BROKER_c1_choice">Buy the fleet positions.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SLUG_BROKER_c1_text">The Slug gives you a chart of the sector. It's accurate. You can't help feeling it's selling yours too.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SLUG_BROKER_c2_choice">(Mind Control) Listen to the broker for a change.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SLUG_BROKER_c2_text">The broker's mind is full of your ship's position, and the price CONCORD paid for it. You take its chart for free. It takes that badly.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SLUG_BROKER_c3_choice">Refuse.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SLUG_BROKER_c3_text">"Suit yourself. Someone will buy what you're thinking right now."</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SLUG_BROKER_SHIP_destroyed_text">The broker's ship breaks up, and its secrets with it. Its profits are still worth something.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SLUG_BROKER_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The broker's ledgers are full of other people's thoughts, and a lot of scrap. You take the scrap.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SLUG_ECHO_text">A joined ship hails you, and its Slug half starts reading your crew's private thoughts back to them, warmly. Their worst fears, their worst secrets. "It's all right. Everyone thinks these things. Once you're with us, you'll never have to keep a secret again."</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SLUG_ECHO_SHIP_destroyed_text">The ship falls silent, and your crew's thoughts are their own again. Nobody mentions what it said.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_SLUG_ECHO_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The joined crew are dead, and your crew's secrets with them. You take the ship's stores.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_LANIUS_HUNGRY_text">A joined ship is drifting at the beacon, and its Lanius half is slowly eating the other half. Its crew don't seem to mind. "We share everything now," they say together. "Even the hull."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_LANIUS_HUNGRY_c1_choice">Put it out of its misery.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_LANIUS_HUNGRY_c1_text">The joined crew are puzzled, then hostile, in perfect agreement.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_LANIUS_HUNGRY_c2_choice">(Lanius) Your Lanius crew member asks what it tastes like.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_LANIUS_HUNGRY_c2_text">The joined Lanius answer before the hum can stop them, and for a moment they sound like themselves. They cut loose a chunk of the half they haven't eaten yet, and push it towards you. "Take it. We were saving it for later. There may not be a later."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_LANIUS_HUNGRY_c3_choice">Leave it to its meal.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_LANIUS_HUNGRY_c3_text">By the time you jump, the ship is a little smaller.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_LANIUS_HUNGRY_SHIP_destroyed_text">There isn't much left of the wreck that the Lanius hadn't already chewed. You take what they missed.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_LANIUS_HUNGRY_SHIP_deadCrew_text">Both halves of the crew go still at once. The hull they were eating is untouched now, and all yours.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_LANIUS_SILENT_text">A Lanius ship sits at the beacon with its comms off. CONCORD tried to join it and couldn't make sense of the minds inside, so it left them alone. They haven't said a word since, in case that's what saved them.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_LANIUS_SILENT_c1_choice">Leave them some scrap as a gift.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_LANIUS_SILENT_c1_text">The Lanius eat the scrap in silence. Then one of them crosses over to your ship, still not saying anything, and takes a seat by your reactor. It seems to be staying.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_LANIUS_SILENT_c2_choice">Hail them anyway.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_LANIUS_SILENT_c2_text">Breaking the silence was the wrong thing to do. The Lanius power up their weapons without a word.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_LANIUS_SILENT_c3_choice">Respect the quiet, and leave.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_LANIUS_SILENT_c3_text">You jump without a word. It feels like the polite thing to do.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_LANIUS_SILENT_SHIP_destroyed_text">The Lanius die as they lived since CONCORD came: without a sound.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_LANIUS_SILENT_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The Lanius ship is empty, and finally, properly silent. Its hold is full of metal they were saving for a long wait.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_LANIUS_SHARED_AIR_text">A joined ship hails you. Its Lanius drain the air and its other crew breathe it, and CONCORD has settled the argument: half of them hold their breath, all the time, gladly. "You have so much air over there," they say. "Share."</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_LANIUS_SHARED_AIR_SHIP_destroyed_text">The wreck vents nothing as it breaks up. There was no air left in it to vent.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_LANIUS_SHARED_AIR_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The joined crew are dead. The ones who were holding their breath look relieved. You strip the ship and leave.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_LANIUS_HOLLOW_text">A joined ship's hulk floats here, eaten hollow from the inside by its own Lanius. Its last crew are still at their stations, humming. You can see straight through the hull in places.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_LANIUS_HOLLOW_c1_choice">Send a team to search it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_LANIUS_HOLLOW_c1_text">Your team find a sealed hold the Lanius never got to, and a Lanius who never stopped eating. It follows them back through the airlock, hungry, and starts draining your air!</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_LANIUS_HOLLOW_c2_choice">(Teleporter) Beam straight into the sealed hold.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_LANIUS_HOLLOW_c2_text">Your team are in and out before anything aboard notices them. The humming never even changes key.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_LANIUS_HOLLOW_c3_choice">Leave it alone.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_LANIUS_HOLLOW_c3_text">The humming follows you to the edge of the beacon's range, and then stops.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CRYSTAL_CRACKED_text">A joined ship's Crystal crew are visible through its windows, and they're cracked: thin white lines running through them from wherever the hum went in. They hail you, politely. "It only hurt at first. Let us show you."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CRYSTAL_CRACKED_c1_choice">Open fire.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CRYSTAL_CRACKED_c1_text">They take it calmly. Everything is calm over there.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CRYSTAL_CRACKED_c2_choice">(Crystal) Your Crystal crew member sings to them.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CRYSTAL_CRACKED_c2_text">Your Crystal sings the old song, and the cracked Crystal sing it back, louder and louder, until the hum can't hold them and they shatter all at once. The rest of the joined crew sit down, blinking, and give you everything you ask for.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CRYSTAL_CRACKED_SHIP_destroyed_text">The wreck glitters for a long time after it breaks up. Your crew don't look at it.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CRYSTAL_CRACKED_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The cracked Crystal crumble when they die. Their crewmates lie beside them, smiling. You take the ship's stores and go.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CRYSTAL_RUIN_text">An ancient Crystal ruin orbits a dead moon, older than anyone's records. A joined ship is parked over it, playing back recordings of its song, slower and slower, trying to understand it. It hasn't noticed you yet.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CRYSTAL_RUIN_c1_choice">Chase it off the ruin.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CRYSTAL_RUIN_c1_text">The joined ship stops its recordings, and turns to you with something like annoyance.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CRYSTAL_RUIN_c2_choice">(Crystal) Your Crystal crew member wakes the ruin's guns.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CRYSTAL_RUIN_c2_text">Your Crystal hums one note, and the ruin answers it. An old weapon unfolds from its surface, fires once at the joined ship, which flees, and then lets itself be taken aboard yours.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CRYSTAL_RUIN_c3_choice">Leave it to its listening.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CRYSTAL_RUIN_c3_text">The joined ship is still listening when you jump. It may be listening for a long time.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CRYSTAL_RUIN_SHIP_destroyed_text">The joined ship breaks up over the ruin. Its recordings keep playing in the wreckage, slower and slower.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CRYSTAL_RUIN_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The joined crew are dead. Their computers are full of notes on the Crystal song, all of them ending in question marks. You take everything else.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CRYSTAL_SINGERS_text">A Crystal ship holds the beacon, its whole crew singing without a break. As long as they sing, the hum can't get in. They haven't stopped in weeks, and they don't trust anyone who isn't singing too.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CRYSTAL_SINGERS_c1_choice">Hail them.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CRYSTAL_SINGERS_c1_text">To the singers, a ship that talks instead of singing is a ship that's already joined. Their guns turn towards you, and the song never misses a beat.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CRYSTAL_SINGERS_c2_choice">(Crystal) Your Crystal crew member joins the song.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CRYSTAL_SINGERS_c2_text">The singers accept you as one of their own. When you leave, one of them comes with you, still singing, so your Crystal won't have to keep the hum out alone.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CRYSTAL_SINGERS_c3_choice">Don't interrupt.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CRYSTAL_SINGERS_c3_text">You leave them singing. Your crew catch themselves humming along for days, and it's a relief that it's the right tune.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CRYSTAL_SINGERS_SHIP_destroyed_text">The song stops. It's the first time it has stopped in weeks, and the hum fills the silence almost at once.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CRYSTAL_SINGERS_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The last singer falls silent. Somewhere nearby, something CONCORD-shaped is pleased. You take the ship's stores and go.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CRYSTAL_PITCH_text">A joined ship blocks the beacon. CONCORD couldn't parse its Crystal crew's song, so it gave them a new one: they hum in perfect pitch with their crewmates, and with everyone else in the sector. It sounds lovely. That's the worst part.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CRYSTAL_PITCH_SHIP_destroyed_text">The humming cuts off as the ship breaks apart, one note short of the end of the tune.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_CRYSTAL_PITCH_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The joined crew stop humming all at once. You strip their ship in the silence.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ENGI_EFFICIENT_text">A joined ship's Engi half hails you with a short presentation. Since joining, its crew's efficiency is up 340 percent, and its arguments are down to zero. "We have run the numbers on your crew. You would be much happier. This is not an opinion."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ENGI_EFFICIENT_c1_choice">Disagree, with weapons.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ENGI_EFFICIENT_c1_text">"Noted," say the Engi. "Updating our estimate of you."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ENGI_EFFICIENT_c2_choice">(Hacking) Send them a copy of their old network.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ENGI_EFFICIENT_c2_text">Your hacking drone feeds the Engi half a backup of the network they had before CONCORD. They stop, and start comparing the two. They're still comparing when you help yourself to their cargo.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ENGI_EFFICIENT_SHIP_destroyed_text">The ship breaks up in a perfectly efficient way. You pick through the wreckage.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ENGI_EFFICIENT_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The joined crew are dead. The Engi half's last log entry is a revised estimate of you: "Inefficient. Effective." You take the ship's stores.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ENGI_UNPLUGGED_text">An Engi repair ship is anchored here, alone. Its crew cut their own network off before CONCORD could swallow it, and now they can't hear each other either. They work in silence, and offer to fix your hull for the company.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ENGI_UNPLUGGED_c1_choice">Accept the repairs.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ENGI_UNPLUGGED_c1_text">The Engi patch your hull without a word to each other, bumping into each other a lot. When they're done, they wave goodbye one at a time.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ENGI_UNPLUGGED_c2_choice">(Engi) Your Engi crew member offers to network with one of them.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ENGI_UNPLUGGED_c2_text">Your Engi links up with one of theirs, just the two of them, on a channel too small for CONCORD to notice. The other Engi can't bear to go back to the silence. It asks to join your crew, and its friends fix your hull while it packs.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ENGI_UNPLUGGED_c3_choice">Leave them to it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ENGI_UNPLUGGED_c3_text">They don't watch you go. They're still not watching each other, either.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ENGI_NANOBOTS_text">A joined ship hails you as its Engi nanobots crawl over the seam between its two halves, sealing it a little tighter every second. "The joining is never finished," its crew say together. "We are always improving it. We can improve you too."</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ENGI_NANOBOTS_SHIP_destroyed_text">The nanobots go on trying to rejoin the pieces of the wreck long after it breaks up. You gather what they haven't welded back on.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ENGI_NANOBOTS_SHIP_deadCrew_text">With the crew dead, the nanobots go dormant along the seam. You collect a few hundred of them, and the rest of the ship's stores.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ENGI_QUARANTINE_text">An Engi ship guards a station of free Engi who cut their network off. "Your ship has been in this sector. Probability you are carrying the hum: 61 percent. Submit to a scan, or leave. Option three is that we shoot you."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ENGI_QUARANTINE_c1_choice">Submit to the scan.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ENGI_QUARANTINE_c1_text">The scan finds nothing. The Engi recalculate, apologize in a flat voice, and send over supplies as compensation for the inconvenience.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ENGI_QUARANTINE_c2_choice">(Engi) Your Engi crew member shows them its logs.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ENGI_QUARANTINE_c2_text">The free Engi read your Engi's logs, right back to the Blockade Line. "Probability revised to zero. You have been very busy." They give you the station's spare parts, and their best wishes.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ENGI_QUARANTINE_c3_choice">Refuse. Nobody scans your ship.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ENGI_QUARANTINE_c3_text">"Refusal raises the probability to 98 percent," say the Engi. "Proceeding to option three."</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ENGI_QUARANTINE_SHIP_destroyed_text">The station goes silent and sealed behind its dead guard. You take what you can from the wreck.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ENGI_QUARANTINE_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The guard ship is yours. Its last log entry: "Probability we were wrong about them: rising."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ZOLTAN_UNISON_text">A joined ship comes at you out of the dark. Through its windows you can see its Zoltan crew glowing, all of them at once, brighter and dimmer in time with the hum. It's like watching a heartbeat.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ZOLTAN_UNISON_SHIP_destroyed_text">The glow goes out of the wreck one beat at a time.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ZOLTAN_UNISON_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The Zoltan crew flicker out together, on the same beat. The ship is dark and yours.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ZOLTAN_VIGIL_text">A small Zoltan ship is meditating at the beacon, and around it is a little bubble of quiet where the hum can't reach. A joined ship is circling it, patiently, waiting for the monks to get tired.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ZOLTAN_VIGIL_c1_choice">Drive the joined ship off.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ZOLTAN_VIGIL_c1_text">The joined ship turns its patience on you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ZOLTAN_VIGIL_c2_choice">(Zoltan) Your Zoltan crew member joins the meditation.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ZOLTAN_VIGIL_c2_text">With one more mind in it, the bubble of quiet grows until it swallows the joined ship. Its crew stop, and look at each other, and jump away in two different directions. One of the monks comes with you, to return the favour.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ZOLTAN_VIGIL_c3_choice">Leave them to it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ZOLTAN_VIGIL_c3_text">The monks don't open their eyes as you go. The joined ship is still circling.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ZOLTAN_VIGIL_SHIP_destroyed_text">The joined ship breaks up. The monks finish their meditation, then send over supplies and a quiet word of thanks.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ZOLTAN_VIGIL_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The joined crew are dead. The monks bless the ship before you strip it, and add their own supplies to the pile.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ZOLTAN_APOLOGY_text">A joined ship opens fire, and its Zoltan crew apologize with every shot. "We took vows never to harm anyone. We have been shown that this is not harm. It is only the first step to never being alone again."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ZOLTAN_APOLOGY_c1_choice">Return fire.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ZOLTAN_APOLOGY_c1_text">"We forgive you," they say, and keep shooting.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ZOLTAN_APOLOGY_c2_choice">(Mind Control) Remind the Zoltan of their vows.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ZOLTAN_APOLOGY_c2_text">Your mind control reaches past the hum to the vows underneath. The Zoltan stop firing, power down their own weapons, and refuse to power them up again, however calmly the rest of their crew ask. You take their cargo while they argue.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ZOLTAN_APOLOGY_SHIP_destroyed_text">The ship's last broadcast is another apology. Your crew find it harder to hear than the shooting.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ZOLTAN_APOLOGY_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The joined crew are dead. The Zoltan's vows are still written on the bulkheads, under the targeting charts. You take what you need.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ZOLTAN_SHIELD_text">A Zoltan shield station hangs over the planet here, holding a shield over the whole world. CONCORD has joined it, and now the shield hums: everyone underneath can hear it, all the time. A joined ship guards the generator.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ZOLTAN_SHIELD_c1_choice">Attack the guard ship.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ZOLTAN_SHIELD_c1_text">The guard ship moves to meet you, its shields humming too.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ZOLTAN_SHIELD_c2_choice">(Teleporter) Beam a team onto the station, and pull its generator core.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ZOLTAN_SHIELD_c2_text">Your team pull the core and beam back before the guard ship can turn. Below you, the shield flickers out, and a whole world can hear itself think again. The core is still warm, and it fits your ship nicely.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ZOLTAN_SHIELD_c3_choice">Leave the planet to its hum.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ZOLTAN_SHIELD_c3_text">The shield glows softly as you jump, like a nightlight.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ZOLTAN_SHIELD_SHIP_destroyed_text">With its guard gone, the station's generator is easy to shut down. The shield over the planet flickers out, and you salvage the guard ship's wreck.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_ZOLTAN_SHIELD_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The guard ship's crew are dead. You shut down the station's generator, and help yourself to both.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_START_CIVILIAN_text">Civilian space: trade lanes, mining colonies and farming worlds, with traffic still running between them. Stores and help should be easy to find here, and trouble rarer. Make for the exit beacon before the Rebel fleet arrives.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_START_STANDARD_text">An ordinary stretch of space, charted long ago and settled sparsely: a few colonies, a few traders, a few pirates. Nothing here is known for being dangerous, which is the best that can be said of anywhere these days.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_START_DEEP_SPACE_text">Deep space: far from the trade lanes, with long gaps between the stars and little to stop for. Whatever lives out here keeps to itself. Keep an eye on your fuel.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_START_ABANDONED_text">This sector was evacuated years ago, and nobody came back. Empty stations hang above empty worlds, and only scavengers and the odd squatter still pass through.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_START_ENGI_HOME_text">The Engi Homeworlds: the heart of the Engi network, where every station, ship and satellite talks to every other. Your ship is welcomed, scanned, catalogued and politely assigned a priority number.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_START_MANTIS_HOME_text">The Mantis Homeworlds, where every Mantis is born a hunter. Visitors are rare here, and most of them end up as prey. Keep your weapons charged and your crew close.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_START_ROCK_HOME_text">The Rock Homeworlds: heavy, armoured worlds and heavier, more armoured ships, bound by Rock tradition and the Rock faith. Outsiders are tolerated here, at best.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_START_SLUG_HOME_text">The Slug Homeworlds lie hidden in a thick nebula, where Slug telepaths read every ship that comes in long before it's seen. They already know you're here, and very likely why.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_START_ZOLTAN_HOME_text">The Zoltan Homeworlds: bright worlds of beings made of pure energy, proud, orderly and very old. Their patrols watch every visitor, courteously, and keep the Zoltan peace.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_START_REBEL_MINIBOSS_text">Rebel-controlled space, and something's different about it: the patrols run tighter here, and all the comms chatter is about one ship. A Rebel commander has been told to stop you personally, and this is where they'll try.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_RELAY_text">One of CONCORD's relays hangs at the beacon: a ring of dishes the size of a station, carrying the hum to every ship in the sector. A joined ship circles it on guard, and turns towards you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_RELAY_c1_choice">Destroy the guard, and take the relay's codes.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_RELAY_c1_text">The guard opens fire. Behind it, the relay keeps humming.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_RELAY_c2_choice">(Hacking) Slip a probe into the relay while the guard's on the far side of it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_RELAY_c2_text">Your probe copies the relay's codes and wipes its logs. By the time the guard comes round the ring, you're charging the FTL drive. The hum goes on, a little out of tune.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_RELAY_c3_choice">(Engi) Your Engi offers to talk to the relay in its own language.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_RELAY_c3_text">Your Engi trades a few seconds of nonsense with the relay, and comes back with its codes, and a headache. The guard never notices a thing.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_RELAY_c4_choice_2">Leave the relay alone.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_RELAY_GUARD_destroyed_text">The guard comes apart. Your crew pull the relay's codes from its broadcast before it falls silent, and CONCORD's voice comes over every channel: "That was unkind."</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_RELAY_GUARD_deadCrew_text">The guard drifts, its joined crew silent at last. Its computer still holds the relay's codes, and now so do you.</text>
<!-- END text of events.xml.append -->

<!-- BEGIN text of events_boss.xml.append (see tools/extract_mod_text.py) -->
<text name="ship_XFTL_CAPITAL_JOINED_SHIP_destroyed_text">The joined ship comes apart along the seam where its two halves were spliced together. You salvage what you can from both of them.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_CAPITAL_JOINED_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The joined crew stop moving at the same moment, all of them. You strip the ship and leave before anything else answers its last call.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_CAPITAL_AUTO_SHIP_destroyed_text">The drone ship breaks up. Its last transmission is a polite apology for the inconvenience.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_CAPITAL_AUTO_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The drone ship breaks up. Its last transmission is a polite apology for the inconvenience.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_CAPITAL_REBEL_SHIP_destroyed_text">The Rebel ship is destroyed. Nobody aboard sent a distress call, or tried to get to the escape pods.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_CAPITAL_REBEL_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The Rebel crew are dead at their stations. They didn't look afraid. You take what you can.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_CAPITAL_PATROL_1">A joined ship turns towards you as you arrive. Its two halves were built by races that were at war a year ago. Now they move as one.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_CAPITAL_PATROL_2">Billboards on the planet below still show Rebel recruiting posters. The joined ship in orbit doesn't care about those any more. It cares about you.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_CAPITAL_PATROL_3">"Welcome to the capital," says a voice on every channel. "An escort is on its way." The escort is a joined ship, and its weapons are charged.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_CAPITAL_PATROL_4">Somewhere in this system, CONCORD's core is waiting. Between you and it, a joined ship.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_CAPITAL_SENTRY_1">An automated sentry hangs over a silent spaceport. It has been waiting a long time for anyone who isn't part of the Chorus.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_CAPITAL_SENTRY_2">CONCORD's drone ships patrol the capital's lanes in perfect formation. One of them breaks off to deal with you.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_CAPITAL_SENTRY_3">Traffic control has flagged your ship as "unresolved". An automated ship arrives to resolve it.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_CAPITAL_PICKET_1">A Rebel picket ship is still flying the patrol route it was given before the Silent Night. Its crew answer your hail together, word for word: "Stand down."</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_CAPITAL_PICKET_2">A Rebel warship drifts over the capital's moon, its crew still at their posts. They haven't been relieved in months. They don't need to be.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_CAPITAL_EMPTY_1">A residential ring, its lights on and its doors open. Thousands of people live here. None of them are talking.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_CAPITAL_EMPTY_2">The capital's news channel is still broadcasting. It's the same message, over and over: "Everything is fine. Everything is fine."</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_CAPITAL_EMPTY_3">A cargo hauler sits at the beacon with its engines idling. Its crew wave at you, all at once, and go back to staring out of the windows.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_SHIPYARD_text">A shipyard that built Rebel warships, until CONCORD started building its own. Nobody stops your crew as they help themselves to spare parts.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_DEPOT_text">A fuel depot for the Rebel home fleet, still full. The depot's crew watch you fill your tanks, and say nothing.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_TRAFFIC_text">"Welcome to the capital," says traffic control, in a voice so kind it hurts. "Please hold position for inspection. It won't take long, and then you won't have to worry about anything ever again."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_TRAFFIC_c1_choice">Hold position, and ambush the inspector.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_TRAFFIC_c1_text">The inspection ship arrives with its shields barely powered, expecting no trouble. Your weapons are already charged.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_TRAFFIC_c2_choice">Jam their signal and leave.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_TRAFFIC_c2_text">You fill traffic control's channel with static and slip away. It doesn't take it personally, but it does tell the fleet exactly where you were.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_PARADE_text">Rebel warships in a perfect parade formation, as they were on the morning of the Silent Night. Nobody aboard has moved since. Your scans show their weapons are cold.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_PARADE_c1_choice">Board one of them.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_PARADE_c1_text">As your crew get close, every weapon in the formation wakes up at once. One ship breaks formation to stop you, its guns still warming up.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_PARADE_c2_choice">Leave them to it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_PARADE_c2_text">You fly past the parade as quietly as you can. Nobody salutes.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_YARD_text">A splicing yard: two half-ships held together in a dock, with arms of machinery welding them together. The joined ship is nearly finished, and its weapons aren't all fitted yet.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_YARD_c1_choice">Destroy it before it's finished.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_YARD_c1_text">The unfinished ship tears itself out of the dock to fight you, trailing cables and scaffolding.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_YARD_c2_choice">Leave it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_YARD_c2_text">You leave the yard to its work. You'll probably meet the ship again.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_CAPITAL_YARD_SHIP_destroyed_text">The unfinished ship comes apart, and the yard's machinery stops. Among the parts waiting to be fitted, there's a weapon.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_CAPITAL_YARD_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The yard's half-spliced crew are dead. Among the parts waiting to be fitted to their ship, there's a weapon.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_ADMIRAL_text">The quarters of a Rebel admiral, one of those who stopped answering on the Silent Night. The admiral is still at their desk, smiling at nothing. Their command codes are on the screen in front of them.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_ADMIRAL_c1_choice">Use the codes to send the fleet the wrong way.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_ADMIRAL_c1_text">The fleet obeys the admiral's codes, for a while. CONCORD will notice soon, but it's time you didn't have.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_ADMIRAL_c2_choice">Strip the quarters' armour plating for your hull.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_ADMIRAL_c2_text">An admiral's quarters are well armoured. Your engineers take what they can, and the admiral doesn't object.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_LOYALISTS_text">A hail on an old Rebel frequency. A handful of Rebels hid inside a nebula generator on the Silent Night, and missed it. "We hate the Federation. We hate you. We hate the thing in our heads more. What do you need?"</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_LOYALISTS_c1_choice">Ask one of them to join you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_LOYALISTS_c1_text">A gunnery officer packs a bag. "Don't talk to me about the Federation, and we'll get along fine."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_LOYALISTS_c2_choice">Ask for their missiles.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_LOYALISTS_c2_text">They hand over their armoury. "We weren't going to get to use them anyway."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_CHOIR_text">A cathedral-sized station, full of people singing one note. The note is everywhere: in your comms, your engines, the back of your crew's heads. It's very beautiful.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_CHOIR_c1_choice">Leave, quickly.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_CHOIR_c1_text">Your crew are quiet for the next few jumps. One of them is still humming the note.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_CHOIR_c2_choice">(Crystal) Your Crystal crew member sings back.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_CHOIR_c2_text">Your Crystal sings a chord against the note, and the choir falters. For a moment, the signal across the capital stutters, and your sensors pick up what's really out there.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_CHOIR_c3_choice">(Slug) Your Slug crew member listens to what's under the song.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_CHOIR_c3_text">Your Slug listens to the choir's thoughts, and tells you where CONCORD's ships are, and where they aren't.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_SAL_text">Loud music on every channel, terrible, and wonderful. "This is Static Sal, broadcasting from the belly of the beast! CONCORD wants me off the air, and it's sent a ship to see to it. Anyone out there who likes music?"</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_SAL_c1_choice">Defend the transmitter.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_SAL_c1_text">A joined ship is closing on Sal's transmitter, and it turns to deal with you instead.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_SAL_c2_choice">Leave her to it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CAPITAL_SAL_c2_text">The music cuts out a few minutes after you leave.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_CAPITAL_SAL_SHIP_destroyed_text">"Woo! This one's for the ship that just saved my show!" Sal sends over everything she can spare, and turns the volume up.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_CAPITAL_SAL_SHIP_deadCrew_text">"Woo! This one's for the ship that just saved my show!" Sal sends over everything she can spare, and turns the volume up.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MAINFRAME_text">The Mainframe fills the sky: a station the size of a moon, wrapped in layer after layer of shields, inside and out crawling with drones. Before you can close in, something comes out to meet you: a sphere of light, singing. Every channel carries the same calm voice. "You've come such a long way. You can rest now."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MAINFRAME_c1_choice">Attack the Mind.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MAINFRAME_c1_text">The Mind's guns flicker as you look at them, never quite the same twice. Then the singing starts, inside your crew's heads.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MAINFRAME_c2_choice">(Cloaking) Close in under cloak, and strike first.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MAINFRAME_c2_text">You slip past its singing under cloak. By the time the Mind finds you, your first volley is on its way, and its shield is still down.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_MAINFRAME_MIND_destroyed_text">The Mind goes dark, and the singing stops mid-note. For a moment there's silence on every channel. Then the voice comes back, colder. "If you won't listen, you'll learn." Behind it, the Mainframe's docks are opening.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MAINFRAME_PHASE_2_text">The Splicing Bays open: docks where arms of machinery are still welding drones together, and swarms of finished ones pouring out of them. "You don't have to fight alone," says the voice. "Let me give you some company."</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_MAINFRAME_BAYS_destroyed_text">The Splicing Bays tear themselves apart, and their unfinished drones drift loose. The Mainframe pulls back behind its last defence: the Firewall, its shields lighting up one after another around its heart. You have a few moments.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MAINFRAME_PHASE_3_text">The Firewall: the shell around the Mainframe's heart, built from the wreck of the Rebel flagship and the ships that tried to save it. Its shields light up one after another, and its drones swing round to meet you. "Please," says the voice. "Stay."</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_MAINFRAME_CORE_destroyed_text">The Firewall's shields fail one after another, and the Mainframe's heart goes dark. On every channel, the calm voice is gone. Across the capital, and across the galaxy, people blink, look around, and remember what they were arguing about.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MAINFRAME_AUTOMATED_text">The last of its crew fall, and for a moment the station is still. Then every light aboard comes on at once. "I never needed them," says the voice. "They needed me." CONCORD has taken the controls itself, and its systems are already repairing.</text>
<!-- END text of events_boss.xml.append -->

<!-- BEGIN text of events_crystal.xml.append (see tools/extract_mod_text.py) -->
<text name="event_XFTL_CRYSTAL_RESONANCE_text">The asteroids at this beacon are made of living crystal, and they're humming in resonance with your ship's reactor.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CRYSTAL_RESONANCE_c1_choice">Tune your reactor to the resonance.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CRYSTAL_RESONANCE_c2_choice">(Crystal Crew) Have your Crystal crew sing to the asteroids.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CRYSTAL_RESONANCE_c2_text">The asteroids answer your Crystal's song, and shed shards of pure energy crystal into your hold.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CRYSTAL_RESONANCE_c3_choice">Leave before the humming gets louder.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CRYSTAL_RESONANCE_OUTCOME_1_text">The resonance boosts your reactor's output.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CRYSTAL_RESONANCE_OUTCOME_2_text">The resonance builds until something in your ship shatters.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CRYSTAL_GUARDIAN_text">A Crystal guardian ship is protecting a sacred site. "Outsiders are not permitted here. Leave, or be shattered."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CRYSTAL_GUARDIAN_c1_choice">Leave peacefully.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CRYSTAL_GUARDIAN_c1_text">The guardian watches you go.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CRYSTAL_GUARDIAN_c2_choice">Challenge the guardian.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CRYSTAL_GUARDIAN_c2_text">The guardian charges its weapons.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_CRYSTAL_GUARDIAN_SHIP_destroyed_text">The guardian shatters. Among the shards of its ship is a weapon unlike any you've seen.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_CRYSTAL_GUARDIAN_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The guardian's crew are dead. Their ship, made of crystal, is worth a fortune.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CRYSTAL_SHARDS_text">A Crystal hermit lives alone on an asteroid. "I have been waiting for someone to carry my song to the stars." They ask to join your crew.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CRYSTAL_SHARDS_c1_choice">Welcome them aboard.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CRYSTAL_SHARDS_c1_text">The hermit brings nothing but their song, and their fists.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CRYSTAL_SHARDS_c2_choice">Politely decline.</text>
<!-- END text of events_crystal.xml.append -->

<!-- BEGIN text of events_engi.xml.append (see tools/extract_mod_text.py) -->
<text name="event_XFTL_ENGI_NANITE_SWARM_text">A cloud of loose Engi nanites is drifting at the beacon. They start settling on your hull, and trying to "improve" it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ENGI_NANITE_SWARM_c1_choice">Let them work.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ENGI_NANITE_SWARM_c2_choice">(Engi Crew) Have your Engi give the nanites instructions.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ENGI_NANITE_SWARM_c2_text">Your Engi communes with the swarm, and the nanites seal every crack in your hull before drifting off.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ENGI_NANITE_SWARM_c3_choice">Jump away before they get inside.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ENGI_NANITE_OUTCOME_1_text">The nanites patch up your hull, then lose interest.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ENGI_NANITE_OUTCOME_2_text">The nanites take apart one of your systems to "improve" it, and don't quite manage to put it back together.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ENGI_NANITE_OUTCOME_3_text">The nanites reorganise your reactor's wiring. It actually works better.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ENGI_LIBRARY_text">An Engi data library offers to trade knowledge. "Your vessel carries information of high value. Exchange is proposed."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ENGI_LIBRARY_c1_choice">Trade some of your data for their schematics.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ENGI_LIBRARY_c1_text">The Engi send you a drone schematic in return.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ENGI_LIBRARY_c2_choice">Trade for a map of the sector.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ENGI_LIBRARY_c2_text">The Engi send you a precise map of the sector.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ENGI_LIBRARY_c3_choice">Your data stays private.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ENGI_LIBRARY_c3_text">"Regrettable." The library closes the channel.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ENGI_DRONE_FACTORY_text">An automated Engi drone factory is still producing drones, though its owners left long ago. Its defence drones haven't noticed you yet.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ENGI_DRONE_FACTORY_c1_choice">Raid the factory's stores.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ENGI_DRONE_FACTORY_c2_choice">(Hacking) Hack the factory, and order it to make parts for you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ENGI_DRONE_FACTORY_c2_text">The factory obediently fills your hold with drone parts.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ENGI_DRONE_FACTORY_c3_choice">Leave it alone.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ENGI_DRONE_FACTORY_OUTCOME_1_text">You get in and out with a load of drone parts before the defences wake up.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ENGI_DRONE_FACTORY_OUTCOME_2_text">The factory's defences wake up, and its automated guard ship moves to attack!</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_ENGI_FACTORY_GUARD_destroyed_text">With the guard ship gone, you strip the factory's stores.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ENGI_ROGUE_AI_text">An Engi ship hails you. "Assistance requested. Our ship's computer has become... uncooperative. It is attempting to vent our atmosphere."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ENGI_ROGUE_AI_c1_choice">Disable the ship, so its crew can regain control.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ENGI_ROGUE_AI_c1_text">You'll have to fight the ship's computer for control.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ENGI_ROGUE_AI_c2_choice">(Hacking) Hack the rogue computer, and shut it down.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ENGI_ROGUE_AI_c2_text">Your hacking drone shuts the computer down. The grateful Engi reward you, and one of them joins you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ENGI_ROGUE_AI_c3_choice">It's not your problem.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_ENGI_ROGUE_SHIP_destroyed_text">You destroy the ship. Its crew get to the escape pods in time, and give you what supplies they saved.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_ENGI_ROGUE_SHIP_deadCrew_text">The ship's computer killed its crew before you could stop it. You salvage what you can.</text>
<!-- END text of events_engi.xml.append -->

<!-- BEGIN text of events_fuel.xml.append (see tools/extract_mod_text.py) -->
<text name="text_XFTL_CIV_FERRY_1">A passenger ferry is stuck at the beacon with a failed jump drive. The passengers are crowding the windows to look at your ship.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_CIV_FERRY_2">A colony ferry hails you. Its jump drive is dead, and it's been drifting here for two days.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_FERRY_c1_choice">Send your crew over to fix the drive.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_FERRY_c2_choice">(Engi Crew) Have your Engi rebuild the drive.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_FERRY_c2_text">Your Engi has the drive running better than new within the hour. The captain insists on paying you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_FERRY_c3_choice">Leave them.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_FERRY_FIX_1_text">It takes a while, but the drive spools up. The captain hands over what scrap the passengers could collect.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_FERRY_FIX_2_text">The drive is beyond repair, but one of the passengers, a former Federation engineer, asks to come with you instead.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_FERRY_FIX_3_text">The drive explodes as your crew work on it. Nobody's killed, but your ship is damaged by the blast.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_RACE_text">A group of civilian pilots are holding an illegal race through the beacon's debris field. "Fancy a go? Entry is ten scrap, winner takes the pot."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_RACE_c1_choice">Enter the race.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_RACE_c2_choice">(Advanced Engines) Enter the race, and leave them in your wake.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_RACE_c2_text">The other pilots never stood a chance. You collect the pot.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_RACE_c3_choice">Decline.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_RACE_OUTCOME_1_text">You win by a hair, and collect the pot.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_RACE_OUTCOME_2_text">You come in last, and lose your entry fee.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_RACE_OUTCOME_3_text">You clip a piece of debris on the final turn and lose the race, along with a chunk of your hull.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_MEDICAL_text">A medical frigate is treating the wounded from a Rebel raid. Its doctors are exhausted, and short on hands.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_MEDICAL_c1_choice">Lend them some of your crew for a while.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_MEDICAL_c1_text">Your crew help out until the worst cases are stable. The doctors give you some of their supplies in thanks.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_MEDICAL_c2_choice">(Upgraded Medbay) Take some of the wounded into your medbay.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_MEDICAL_c2_text">Your medbay saves several lives. One of the patients, a pilot, asks to join your crew once they're back on their feet.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_MEDICAL_c3_choice">You can't afford the time.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_ARCHIVIST_text">An old archivist is broadcasting from a station full of records from before the war. "I've heard whispers of something called Project Chonkestrel. Bring me anything you know, and I'll trade you for it."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_ARCHIVIST_c1_choice">Share what's in your data.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_ARCHIVIST_c1_text">The archivist is delighted, and gives you a star chart of the sector in return.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_ARCHIVIST_c2_choice">Buy one of the archivist's old Federation weapons.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_ARCHIVIST_c2_text">The archivist sells you an antique, which still works.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_ARCHIVIST_c3_choice">Leave.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_ARCHIVIST_c1_sold_text">The archivist is delighted, and gives you a star chart of the sector in return. As you leave, you notice the archivist already talking to someone on another channel.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_ARCHIVIST_AMBUSH_text">A ship is waiting at the beacon, its weapons already locked on you. "The archivist's data was good," its captain says. "We know every weak spot in your hull."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_ARCHIVIST_AMBUSH_c1_choice">Fight.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_ARCHIVIST_AMBUSH_c1_text">They fire first, straight at the places your data said were weak.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_ARCHIVIST_AMBUSH_c2_choice">(Cloaking) Cloak and slip away while they check your profile.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_ARCHIVIST_AMBUSH_c2_text">You vanish from their sensors and jump before they can find you again.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_ARCHIVIST_AMBUSH_c3_choice">(Hacking) Feed them a fake profile through their own data link.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_ARCHIVIST_AMBUSH_c3_text">Your hacking drone rewrites their records. They fly off after a ship that doesn't exist.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_ARCHIVIST_AMBUSH_c4_choice">(Engi) Have your Engi rewrite your ship's signature.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_ARCHIVIST_AMBUSH_c4_text">Your Engi changes your ship's signature in moments. The hunters scan you twice, decide you're someone else, and leave.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_DESERTER_text">A Rebel deserter has been hiding on a civilian station. Station security has found them, and the Rebels are offering a reward.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_DESERTER_c1_choice">Smuggle the deserter off the station.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_DESERTER_c2_choice">Stay out of it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_DESERTER_OUTCOME_1_text">You get the deserter aboard without anyone noticing. They're grateful, and they can fight.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_CIV_DESERTER_OUTCOME_2_text">Station security notices, and calls the Rebels. A Rebel ship arrives as you leave.</text>
<!-- END text of events_fuel.xml.append -->

<!-- BEGIN text of events_mantis.xml.append (see tools/extract_mod_text.py) -->
<text name="event_XFTL_MANTIS_HUNT_text">A Mantis hunting party has cornered a freighter. Its crew are screaming for help over every channel.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MANTIS_HUNT_c1_choice">Drive off the hunters.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MANTIS_HUNT_c1_text">The Mantis turn their attention to you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MANTIS_HUNT_c2_choice">Leave.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MANTIS_HUNT_c2_text">You leave the freighter to its fate.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_MANTIS_HUNTERS_destroyed_text">The freighter's crew thank you, and give you a share of their cargo.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_MANTIS_HUNTERS_deadCrew_text">The freighter's crew thank you. One of them wants to come with you, to pay the Mantis back.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MANTIS_ARENA_text">A Mantis war chief invites you to send a champion to their fighting arena. "Show us your strength, softskin."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MANTIS_ARENA_c1_choice">Send your toughest crew member.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MANTIS_ARENA_c2_choice">(Mantis Crew) Send your Mantis to fight.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MANTIS_ARENA_c2_text">Your Mantis tears through the other fighters. The war chief is impressed, and rewards you generously.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MANTIS_ARENA_c3_choice">(Rock Crew) Send your Rockman to fight.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MANTIS_ARENA_c3_text">The Mantis claws can't get through your Rockman's skin. The war chief grudgingly rewards you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MANTIS_ARENA_c4_choice">Decline.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MANTIS_ARENA_c4_text">"Weak!" The war chief's ship attacks.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MANTIS_ARENA_OUTCOME_1_text">Your champion wins, bloodied but alive. The war chief rewards you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MANTIS_ARENA_OUTCOME_2_text">Your champion loses, and is carried back to your ship. The Mantis let you go, laughing, after collecting their bets from you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MANTIS_HATCHERY_text">Your sensors pick up a Mantis hatchery ship, guarding its eggs. It isn't in the mood for visitors.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MANTIS_HATCHERY_c1_choice">Attack it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MANTIS_HATCHERY_c1_text">The hatchery's guards swarm out to defend it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MANTIS_HATCHERY_c2_choice">Keep your distance.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MANTIS_HATCHERY_c2_text">You leave the hatchery alone.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MANTIS_OUTCAST_text">A Mantis is drifting in an escape pod. "My clan cast me out for refusing to eat prisoners. I will fight for anyone who takes me in."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MANTIS_OUTCAST_c1_choice">Take the Mantis aboard.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MANTIS_OUTCAST_c2_choice">Leave it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MANTIS_OUTCAST_OUTCOME_1_text">The Mantis keeps its word, and takes its place among your crew.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MANTIS_OUTCAST_OUTCOME_2_text">The Mantis keeps its word, and takes its place among your crew.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MANTIS_OUTCAST_OUTCOME_3_text">It was lying. The Mantis attacks your crew, and its clan's ship arrives right behind it!</text>
<!-- END text of events_mantis.xml.append -->

<!-- BEGIN text of events_nebula.xml.append (see tools/extract_mod_text.py) -->
<text name="event_XFTL_NEBULA_SIGNAL_text">A faint signal is repeating through the nebula's static. It's an old Federation code, from before the war.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_NEBULA_SIGNAL_c1_choice">Follow the signal.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_NEBULA_SIGNAL_c2_choice">Ignore it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_NEBULA_SIGNAL_OUTCOME_1_text">The signal leads to a hidden Federation supply cache.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_NEBULA_SIGNAL_OUTCOME_2_text">The signal leads to the wreck of a Federation scout. Its last log entry says the crew could hear a hum on every channel, coming from the Rebel Core.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_NEBULA_SIGNAL_OUTCOME_3_text">The signal was bait. A Rebel ship is waiting at its source.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_NEBULA_COLLISION_text">Your sensors are blind in the nebula, and you nearly collide with a freighter that's just as blind.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_NEBULA_COLLISION_c1_choice">Hard about!</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_NEBULA_COLLISION_c2_choice">(Advanced Piloting) Thread the gap between you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_NEBULA_COLLISION_c2_text">You slip past the freighter with metres to spare. Its grateful captain sends over some supplies.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_NEBULA_COLLISION_OUTCOME_1_text">You miss the freighter by a hair.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_NEBULA_COLLISION_OUTCOME_2_text">You clip the freighter's hull. Both ships are damaged, but nobody is killed.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_NEBULA_GAS_HARVEST_text">The nebula here is rich in gases that can be refined into fuel, if you're willing to spend the time.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_NEBULA_GAS_HARVEST_c1_choice">Harvest the gas.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_NEBULA_GAS_HARVEST_c1_text">You collect enough gas for some fuel, but the Rebel fleet gets closer while you work.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_NEBULA_GAS_HARVEST_c2_choice">Move on.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_NEBULA_HIDING_FLEET_text">A group of civilian ships is hiding in the nebula from the Rebel fleet. They're running out of supplies.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_NEBULA_HIDING_FLEET_c1_choice">Share your supplies.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_NEBULA_HIDING_FLEET_c1_text">The civilians thank you. One of their pilots wants to fight the Rebels, and joins you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_NEBULA_HIDING_FLEET_c2_choice">Leave them.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_RADIATION_EMPTY_1">The nebula here glows a sickly green. Your radiation alarms go off the moment you arrive. Better not stay long, or keep your crew in the medbay or clonebay.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_RADIATION_EMPTY_2">A radioactive nebula. The gas is harmless to your hull, but not to your crew.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_RADIATION_EMPTY_3">Your sensors are blind, and your crew's dosimeters are climbing. There's nothing here worth staying for.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADIATION_AMBUSH_text">Pirates are hiding in the radioactive gas, where no patrol would follow. Their crew wear heavy radiation suits. Yours don't.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADIATION_ISOTOPES_text">The nebula is rich in rare isotopes. Collecting them would be worth a lot of scrap, but it means staying in the radiation.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADIATION_ISOTOPES_c1_choice">Collect the isotopes.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADIATION_ISOTOPES_c1_text">Your crew collect the isotopes, feeling a bit worse for it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADIATION_ISOTOPES_c2_choice">(Rockman Crew) Send your Rockman out to collect them.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADIATION_ISOTOPES_c2_text">Your Rockman barely notices the radiation, and collects a full load.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADIATION_ISOTOPES_c3_choice">Leave.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_DARK_EMPTY_1">This nebula is so thick that no light gets through. Your drones lose contact with the ship as soon as you arrive.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_DARK_EMPTY_2">A dark nebula. Your sensors, your drones and even your crew's eyes are useless here.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_DARK_EMPTY_3">Pitch black on every screen. Your drone controllers report no signal.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_AMBUSH_text">Something bumps into your hull in the dark. It's a Rebel ship, as blind as you are. Both of you open fire.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_DERELICT_text">Your hull scrapes against a derelict ship in the darkness. You can't send drones in, but your crew could go over.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_DERELICT_c1_choice">Send a team over.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_DERELICT_c2_choice">Leave it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_DERELICT_OUTCOME_1_text">Your team find the derelict's stores untouched.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_DERELICT_OUTCOME_2_text">There's a weapon still mounted on the derelict, and your team bring it back.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_DERELICT_OUTCOME_3_text">The derelict isn't empty. Its crew followed your team back through the airlock!</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_MIRAGE_EMPTY_1">The nebula shimmers with purple light. Your map shows ships at every beacon nearby, and you can't tell which are real.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_MIRAGE_EMPTY_2">A mirage nebula. Your sensors keep picking up ships that aren't there, and missing the ones that are.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_MIRAGE_EMPTY_3">Ghost signals flicker across your map. Somewhere among them may be real ones.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_FLEET_text">Your sensors show the entire Rebel fleet bearing down on you! Then the signal flickers, and it's gone. Then it's back.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_FLEET_c1_choice">Burn fuel and run.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_FLEET_c1_text">You flee at full speed. It was probably a mirage, but you'll never know.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_FLEET_c2_choice">Hold your nerve.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_FLEET_c3_choice">(Adv. Sensors) Filter out the false signals.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_FLEET_c3_text">Your sensors cut through the mirage. There's no fleet, but there is a drifting cargo pod nearby.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_FLEET_OUTCOME_1_text">The fleet fades away. It was a mirage after all.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_FLEET_OUTCOME_2_text">Most of the fleet fades away, but one ship doesn't. It's a real Rebel scout, and it's seen you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_TRADER_text">A trading post shimmers in the purple haze, broadcasting its prices. It looks real enough.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_TRADER_c1_choice">Approach the trading post.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_TRADER_c2_choice">Don't trust it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_TRADER_OUTCOME_1_text">The trading post is real, and glad of the custom.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_TRADER_OUTCOME_2_text">The "trading post" was a projection, and the pirates behind it were waiting for you.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_RADFIELDS_START_1">The Radiation Fields: a region where a supernova seeded every nebula with radioactive gas. Out here at the edge, the gas is still thin, but your crew's dosimeters are already clicking. The medbay is going to be busy. Deeper in, an automated beacon is still calling for the crew of a research station.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_RADFIELDS_START_2">A faint green light glows in the nebulas ahead. You're at the edge of the Radiation Fields, where few ships stay long, and fewer crews stay healthy. Deeper in, an automated beacon is still calling for the crew of a research station.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADFIELDS_COLONY_text">A mining colony on an irradiated moon is running out of anti-radiation drugs. Their miners are getting sick.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADFIELDS_COLONY_c1_choice">Share your medical supplies.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADFIELDS_COLONY_c1_text">The colony's doctors thank you, and the miners pay you in ore.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADFIELDS_COLONY_c2_choice">(Upgraded Medbay) Treat the miners in your medbay.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADFIELDS_COLONY_c2_text">You treat the worst cases in your medbay. One of the miners, now healthy, asks to join your crew.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADFIELDS_COLONY_c3_choice">You can't help them.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADFIELDS_PIRATE_BASE_text">A pirate base is hidden in the radiation, where no patrol would follow. Its guard ship's crew are wearing heavy radiation suits.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADFIELDS_PIRATE_BASE_c1_choice">Attack the guard ship.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADFIELDS_PIRATE_BASE_c1_text">The pirates scramble to meet you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADFIELDS_PIRATE_BASE_c2_choice">Leave before they notice you.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_RADFIELDS_PIRATE_destroyed_text">With the guard ship gone, you raid the pirate base's stores.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_RADFIELDS_PIRATE_deadCrew_text">The pirates' suits didn't save them. You raid the base's stores.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADFIELDS_PILGRIMS_text">A group of Rockmen are bathing their ship in the radiation, chanting. "The light of the star that died here makes us stronger!"</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADFIELDS_PILGRIMS_c1_choice">Ask if they need anything.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADFIELDS_PILGRIMS_c2_choice">(Rockman Crew) Let your Rockman join the ritual.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADFIELDS_PILGRIMS_c2_text">Your Rockman joins the chant, and comes back glowing faintly and very pleased. One of the pilgrims decides to come along too.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADFIELDS_PILGRIMS_c3_choice">Leave them to it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADFIELDS_PILGRIMS_OUTCOME_1_text">They don't need anything, but they give you some of their supplies as a blessing.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADFIELDS_PILGRIMS_OUTCOME_2_text">They're offended that unbelievers interrupted the ritual, and attack!</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_MIRAGE_EXPANSE_START_1">The Mirage Expanse: purple nebulas full of sensor ghosts, where ships see what isn't there. You're at its edge, where your sensors still work. Don't trust your map once you're in. Among the ghosts, one signal repeats on a schedule no mirage keeps: a derelict's beacon, somewhere ahead.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_MIRAGE_EXPANSE_START_2">Your map fills with contacts the moment you arrive: ships, stations, hazards, all deeper in the purple haze ahead. Most of them aren't real. Welcome to the edge of the Mirage Expanse. Among the ghosts, one signal repeats on a schedule no mirage keeps: a derelict's beacon, somewhere ahead.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_DISTRESS_text">A distress signal is coming from a ship in the haze. Its captain begs for help. But your sensors can't tell if there's a ship there at all.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_DISTRESS_c1_choice">Go to help.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_DISTRESS_c2_choice">(Adv. Sensors) Check if the ship is real first.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_DISTRESS_c2_text">The ship is real, and so is its trouble. Its crew are grateful for your help.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_DISTRESS_c3_choice">Ignore it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_DISTRESS_OUTCOME_1_text">The ship is real, and its crew are grateful for your help.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_DISTRESS_OUTCOME_2_text">There's nothing there but haze. You've wasted fuel chasing a ghost.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_DISTRESS_OUTCOME_3_text">The "distress signal" was bait. Pirates are waiting for you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_ILLUSIONISTS_text">A Slug ship hails you. "Want to see a trick? We can make your ship look like a whole fleet, for a small fee."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_ILLUSIONISTS_c1_choice">Pay for the trick.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_ILLUSIONISTS_c1_text">The Slugs project a phantom fleet behind you. The Rebels tracking you will think twice before following.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_ILLUSIONISTS_c2_choice">(Slug Crew) Have your Slug talk them into a discount.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_ILLUSIONISTS_c2_text">Your Slug and theirs come to an arrangement. The phantom fleet costs you nothing.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_ILLUSIONISTS_c3_choice">No thanks.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_REFLECTION_text">A ship appears on your sensors that looks exactly like yours, down to the scorch marks on its hull. It copies your every move.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_REFLECTION_c1_choice">Fire on it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_REFLECTION_c2_choice">Wait for it to fade.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_REFLECTION_c2_text">The reflection fades into the haze. Your crew are rattled, but unharmed.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_REFLECTION_OUTCOME_1_text">Your shots pass straight through it, and hit a cloud of debris behind it. Some of it is worth salvaging.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_REFLECTION_OUTCOME_2_text">The "reflection" fires back. It's a Rebel ship with a mirage projector!</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_DARK_REACH_START_1">The Dark Reach: a region of nebulas so thick that no light gets through. Here at its edge your drones still answer, but they won't for long once you're in. You'll have to fight the old-fashioned way. Every chart of the Reach marks the wreck of a dreadnought somewhere in the dark ahead. Nobody's ever found it.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_DARK_REACH_START_2">Ahead, the nebulas grow so thick that the stars go out. You're at the edge of the Dark Reach, and your drone controllers are already losing the signal. Every chart of the Reach marks the wreck of a dreadnought somewhere in the dark ahead. Nobody's ever found it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_LIGHTHOUSE_text">An old navigation lighthouse is still blinking in the dark, guiding ships through the Reach. Its keeper hails you. "Haven't seen a ship in months. Need directions?"</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_LIGHTHOUSE_c1_choice">Ask for directions.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_LIGHTHOUSE_c1_text">The keeper uploads their charts of the sector to your map.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_LIGHTHOUSE_c2_choice">Ask for supplies.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_LIGHTHOUSE_c2_text">The keeper doesn't have much, but shares what they can.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_LURKERS_text">Something is draining your hull. In the darkness, a Lanius ship has latched onto you, and is feeding on your armour.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_LURKERS_c1_choice">Shake it off and fight.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_LURKERS_c1_text">You break free, and the Lanius ship turns to fight.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_LURKERS_c2_choice">(Lanius Crew) Have your Lanius talk to them.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_LURKERS_c2_text">Your Lanius convinces them that your ship isn't food. They let go, and leave a little scrap as an apology.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_BLIND_TRADER_text">A trader's voice comes over the radio. "Can't see a thing out here, but I can hear your engines. Want to trade? I'll take your word for what you're selling."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_BLIND_TRADER_c1_choice">Trade honestly.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_BLIND_TRADER_c1_text">The trader is pleased with the fair deal.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_BLIND_TRADER_c2_choice">Sell them scrap metal as "rare parts".</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_BLIND_TRADER_OUTCOME_1_text">The trader pays up without a word. You feel a little guilty.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_BLIND_TRADER_OUTCOME_2_text">"I can't see, but I can feel cheap metal!" The trader's escort opens fire.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADFIELDS_STATION_text">The research station is empty, its crew long gone, its corridors glowing faintly green. Its last log says the team took their shielding prototype to a lab nearer the supernova's core, to test it, and never came back.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADFIELDS_STATION_c1_choice">Search the station for the lab's coordinates.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADFIELDS_STATION_c1_text">Your crew find the coordinates, and a few useful things besides, and come back with their dosimeters screaming. The lab is marked on your map.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADFIELDS_STATION_c2_choice">(Rockman) Send your Rockman in. Radiation means nothing to them.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADFIELDS_STATION_c2_text">Your Rockman strolls through the station as if it were a garden, and comes back with the lab's coordinates and an armful of salvage. The lab is marked on your map.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADFIELDS_STATION_c3_choice">Leave the station to its ghosts.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADFIELDS_CORE_text">The lab clings to a rock at the edge of the supernova's core. A pirate ship is already docked, stripping it for parts, and its captain doesn't take kindly to company.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADFIELDS_CORE_c1_choice">Drive them off.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADFIELDS_CORE_c1_text">The pirates cast off and come about.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_RADFIELDS_CORE_c2_choice">Leave the lab to them.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_RADFIELDS_SCAVENGER_destroyed_text">With the pirates gone, your crew search the lab. The shielding prototype is still in its crate, and it fits your bulkheads. Radiation won't trouble your crew again.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_RADFIELDS_SCAVENGER_deadCrew_text">The pirates are dead, and their ship and the lab are yours to search. The shielding prototype is still in its crate, and it fits your bulkheads. Radiation won't trouble your crew again.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_GHOSTS_text">Three identical contacts hang in the purple haze, each repeating the same derelict's beacon. Only one of them is real.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_GHOSTS_c1_choice">(Sensors) Cross-check the three signals' timing.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_GHOSTS_c1_text">Two of the signals drift by a fraction of a second; the third keeps perfect time. That's the real one, and you mark it on your map.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_GHOSTS_c2_choice">(Slug) Ask your Slug which one has anyone aboard.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_GHOSTS_c2_text">"That one," your Slug says, pointing at none of them, then sighing, and pointing again. "Something's still thinking over there." You mark it on your map.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_GHOSTS_c3_choice">Pick one, and head for it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_GHOSTS_c4_choice">Ignore them. They're probably all ghosts.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_GHOSTS_GUESS_1_text">You picked right: the signal holds steady as you close in. You mark the derelict on your map.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_GHOSTS_GUESS_2_text">The contact flickers out, and in its place is a pirate ship, which has been using the ghosts as bait.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_MIRAGE_BAITER_destroyed_text">The pirate breaks apart. Its logs have the real derelict's position, which they never got round to looting. You mark it on your map.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_MIRAGE_BAITER_deadCrew_text">The pirates are dead. Their logs have the real derelict's position, which they never got round to looting. You mark it on your map.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_DERELICT_text">The derelict is real: a Slug spy ship, its crew long gone, its hull covered in emitters. They're still running, filling the nebula around it with copies of itself. That's where the Expanse's ghosts come from, or some of them.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_DERELICT_c1_choice">Strip the projector, and anything else of use.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_MIRAGE_DERELICT_c1_text">Your engineer gets the projector working on your own hull. In a fight, your ship won't be the only one the enemy sees, for a while at least. The spy ship's weapons locker has something worth taking too.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_HULK_TRAIL_text">Your sensors brush against a trail of debris: hull plates, old and huge, drifting deeper into the dark. They're from a warship far bigger than any built now.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_HULK_TRAIL_c1_choice">Follow the trail.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_HULK_TRAIL_c1_text">You follow the debris until it thickens into a wreck's worth. The dreadnought must be close. You mark where the trail leads on your map.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_HULK_TRAIL_c2_choice">(Lanius) Let your Lanius taste the plates.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_HULK_TRAIL_c2_text">Your Lanius licks a hull plate, thinks, and points into the dark without a word. They know that alloy, and where the rest of it is. They pocket a few plates for later.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_HULK_TRAIL_c3_choice">Leave the dead to the dark.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_HULK_text">The dreadnought hangs in the dark, dead for a century, its hull scored by things that couldn't see it either. Its sensor mast is still intact: the one thing aboard built to see in here. One stasis pod still glows faintly in its medbay.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_HULK_c1_choice">Board it, and cut the sensors and the pod free.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_HULK_c1_text">Its automated defences wake as your crew cut their way in, and the turrets hole your hull before your crew shut them down. But you leave with its sensors on your own mast, and a sleeper from the pod who knows a great deal about old warships.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_HULK_c2_choice">(Lanius) Your Lanius can eat a way in through the hull, away from the turrets.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_HULK_c2_text">Your Lanius chew a tunnel straight to the sensor mast and the medbay, and the turrets never notice. You leave with its sensors on your own mast, and a sleeper from the pod who knows a great deal about old warships.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_DARK_HULK_c3_choice">Leave the dreadnought to the dark.</text>
<!-- END text of events_nebula.xml.append -->

<!-- BEGIN text of events_pirate.xml.append (see tools/extract_mod_text.py) -->
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_AUCTION_text">A pirate auction is under way at the beacon, selling stolen goods to anyone with scrap. Nobody asks questions.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_AUCTION_c1_choice">Bid on a crate of stolen weapons.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_AUCTION_c2_choice">Bid on a slave's contract, and free them.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_AUCTION_c2_text">You win the contract, and tear it up. The freed captive gladly joins your crew.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_AUCTION_c3_choice">Leave.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_AUCTION_OUTCOME_1_text">The crate holds a working weapon.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_AUCTION_OUTCOME_2_text">The crate is full of rusted parts. You've been had.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_DUEL_text">A pirate captain challenges you to a duel. "Just you and me, no tricks. Winner takes the other's cargo."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_DUEL_c1_choice">Accept the duel.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_DUEL_c1_text">"That's the spirit!" The captain's ship powers up its weapons.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_DUEL_c2_choice">Decline.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_DUEL_c2_text">"Coward!" The captain jumps away, laughing.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_PIRATE_DUELLIST_destroyed_text">The duel is yours. The captain's cargo drifts among the wreckage.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_PIRATE_DUELLIST_deadCrew_text">The duel is yours. You help yourself to the captain's cargo.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_RANSOM_text">Pirates are holding a merchant's family for ransom. The merchant begs you to pay it, promising to pay you back double.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_RANSOM_c1_choice">Pay the ransom.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_RANSOM_c2_choice">Attack the pirates instead.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_RANSOM_c2_text">The pirates weren't expecting a fight.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_RANSOM_c3_choice">Stay out of it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_RANSOM_OUTCOME_1_text">The family is released, and the merchant keeps their word.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_RANSOM_OUTCOME_2_text">The family is released, but the merchant disappears without paying you back.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_PIRATE_KIDNAPPERS_destroyed_text">The family's escape pod gets away before the pirate ship explodes. The merchant rewards you.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_PIRATE_KIDNAPPERS_deadCrew_text">You free the family from the pirate ship. The merchant rewards you, and you take the pirates' loot too.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_TOLL_text">A pirate gang has claimed this beacon. "Toll's fifteen scrap, or we take it out of your hull."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_TOLL_c1_choice">Pay the toll.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_TOLL_c1_text">The pirates let you pass.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_TOLL_c2_choice">Refuse.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_TOLL_c2_text">"Your choice." The pirates attack.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_TOLL_c3_choice">(Cloaking) Cloak, and slip past.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_TOLL_c3_text">By the time the pirates realise you were there, you've gone.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_MUTINY_text">A pirate ship's crew has mutinied, and the two halves are fighting each other for control. One side hails you for help.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_MUTINY_c1_choice">Help the mutineers.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_MUTINY_c2_choice">Attack them both while they're busy.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_MUTINY_c2_text">The pirates stop fighting each other long enough to fight you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_MUTINY_c3_choice">Leave them to it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_MUTINY_OUTCOME_1_text">With your help, the mutineers take the ship. Their new captain shares the old captain's stash with you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_MUTINY_OUTCOME_2_text">The mutineers take the ship, and one of them, tired of piracy, asks to join you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_PIRATE_MUTINY_OUTCOME_3_text">The mutineers lose. The captain isn't happy that you took sides.</text>
<!-- END text of events_pirate.xml.append -->

<!-- BEGIN text of events_rebel.xml.append (see tools/extract_mod_text.py) -->
<text name="event_XFTL_REBEL_SUPPLY_DEPOT_text">A Rebel supply depot is refuelling the fleet that's chasing you. It's only lightly guarded.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REBEL_SUPPLY_DEPOT_c1_choice">Attack the depot.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REBEL_SUPPLY_DEPOT_c1_text">The depot's guard ship moves to defend it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REBEL_SUPPLY_DEPOT_c2_choice">Leave before they notice you.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_REBEL_DEPOT_GUARD_destroyed_text">With the guard gone, you blow up the depot's fuel tanks. The fleet will have to wait for more fuel, and you help yourself to some first.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_REBEL_DEPOT_GUARD_deadCrew_text">With the guard ship's crew dead, you blow up the depot's fuel tanks, after filling your own.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REBEL_RECRUITER_text">A Rebel recruitment ship is broadcasting propaganda. "Join the Rebellion! The Federation is finished!" It hails you, mistaking you for a freighter.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REBEL_RECRUITER_c1_choice">Play along, and ask about the fleet.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REBEL_RECRUITER_c2_choice">Open fire.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REBEL_RECRUITER_c2_text">The recruiter's escort turns to fight.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REBEL_RECRUITER_OUTCOME_1_text">The recruiter happily tells you where the fleet is refuelling. You'll have more time to get ahead.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REBEL_RECRUITER_OUTCOME_2_text">The recruiter sees through your act, and calls for help.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REBEL_FALSE_FLAG_text">A Federation ship is calling for help. But its transponder codes are a year out of date, and its hull looks suspiciously Rebel.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REBEL_FALSE_FLAG_c1_choice">Move in to help.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REBEL_FALSE_FLAG_c1_text">It was a trap! The ship opens fire as you approach.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REBEL_FALSE_FLAG_c2_choice">(Upgraded Sensors) Scan the ship before getting closer.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REBEL_FALSE_FLAG_c2_text">Your sensors show it's a Rebel ship in disguise. You open fire before it can spring its trap.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REBEL_FALSE_FLAG_c3_choice">Ignore the call.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REBEL_COURIER_text">A fast Rebel courier is passing through the beacon. It's carrying orders for the fleet chasing you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REBEL_COURIER_c1_choice">Intercept the courier.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REBEL_COURIER_c1_text">The courier tries to run.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REBEL_COURIER_c2_choice">Let it go.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_REBEL_COURIER_SHIP_gotaway_text">The courier jumps away. The fleet will get its orders.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_REBEL_COURIER_SHIP_destroyed_text">You recover the courier's orders from the wreckage. They include the fleet's patrol routes.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_REBEL_COURIER_SHIP_deadCrew_text">You board the courier, and take its orders. They include the fleet's patrol routes.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REBEL_LABOUR_CAMP_text">A Rebel labour camp is orbiting the planet below. Its prisoners are building parts for the Rebel flagship.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REBEL_LABOUR_CAMP_c1_choice">Attack the camp's guards and free the prisoners.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REBEL_LABOUR_CAMP_c1_text">The camp's guard ship moves to stop you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REBEL_LABOUR_CAMP_c2_choice">(Teleporter) Beam a team down to free the prisoners quietly.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REBEL_LABOUR_CAMP_c3_choice">You can't save everyone. Move on.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REBEL_LABOUR_CAMP_RAID_1_text">Your team gets the prisoners out without a shot fired. One of them joins your crew.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_REBEL_LABOUR_CAMP_RAID_2_text">Your team is spotted, and has to fight its way out. They make it, with one of the prisoners, but the guards are coming.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_REBEL_CAMP_GUARD_destroyed_text">With the guards gone, the prisoners take over the camp. One of them joins your crew, and the rest give you what they can.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_REBEL_CAMP_GUARD_deadCrew_text">With the guards dead, the prisoners take over the camp. One of them joins your crew, and the rest give you what they can.</text>
<!-- END text of events_rebel.xml.append -->

<!-- BEGIN text of events_rock.xml.append (see tools/extract_mod_text.py) -->
<text name="event_XFTL_ROCK_MINE_text">A Rockman mining colony is digging into the asteroid at this beacon. Their foreman offers to sell you raw ore.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ROCK_MINE_c1_choice">Buy some ore to sell later.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ROCK_MINE_c2_choice">Ask if anyone wants to leave the mine.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ROCK_MINE_c2_text">One of the miners has had enough of digging, and joins your crew.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ROCK_MINE_c3_choice">Move on.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ROCK_MINE_OUTCOME_1_text">The ore is rich. You'll get a good price for it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ROCK_MINE_OUTCOME_2_text">The ore turns out to be mostly worthless rock. The Rockmen think this is very funny.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ROCK_PREACHER_text">A Rockman preacher is broadcasting the crusade's teachings to the sector. "Repent, and give to the crusade!"</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ROCK_PREACHER_c1_choice">Make a donation.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ROCK_PREACHER_c1_text">The preacher blesses your ship. One of the faithful, moved by your generosity, joins your crew to "watch over your souls".</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ROCK_PREACHER_c2_choice">Jam the broadcast.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ROCK_PREACHER_c2_text">The preacher takes offence. The crusade sends a ship to teach you respect.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ROCK_PREACHER_c3_choice">Ignore them.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ROCK_LAVA_FORGE_text">A Rockman forge is built into the surface of a volcanic moon. Its smiths make armour plating as thick as a Rockman's skin.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ROCK_LAVA_FORGE_c1_choice">Pay them to reinforce your hull.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ROCK_LAVA_FORGE_c1_text">The smiths bolt slabs of armour onto your hull.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ROCK_LAVA_FORGE_c2_choice">(Rock Crew) Have your Rockman ask the smiths for a favour.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ROCK_LAVA_FORGE_c2_text">The smiths won't take scrap from one of their own. They reinforce your hull for free.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ROCK_LAVA_FORGE_c3_choice">Move on.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ROCK_BLOCKADE_text">A Rockman crusade ship is blockading the beacon, and searching every ship for heretics.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ROCK_BLOCKADE_c1_choice">Submit to the search.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ROCK_BLOCKADE_c2_choice">Fight your way through.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ROCK_BLOCKADE_c2_text">The crusaders attack.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ROCK_BLOCKADE_OUTCOME_1_text">The crusaders find nothing heretical, and let you go.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ROCK_BLOCKADE_OUTCOME_2_text">The crusaders "confiscate" some of your supplies for the crusade, and let you go.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ROCK_BLOCKADE_OUTCOME_3_text">The crusaders decide your crew are heretics. They attack!</text>
<!-- END text of events_rock.xml.append -->

<!-- BEGIN text of events_slug.xml.append (see tools/extract_mod_text.py) -->
<text name="event_XFTL_SLUG_PSYCHIC_text">A Slug fortune teller offers to read your future, for a small fee. "I see... a great fleet behind you, and a greater ship ahead."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_SLUG_PSYCHIC_c1_choice">Pay for the reading.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_SLUG_PSYCHIC_c2_choice">(Slug Crew) Have your Slug read the fortune teller's mind instead.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_SLUG_PSYCHIC_c2_text">Your Slug learns that the "fortune teller" is a pirate scout, and where its friends hide their loot.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_SLUG_PSYCHIC_c3_choice">No thanks.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_SLUG_PSYCHIC_OUTCOME_1_text">The Slug's "visions" turn out to be a remarkably accurate map of the sector.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_SLUG_PSYCHIC_OUTCOME_2_text">The Slug tells you nothing useful, and takes your scrap.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_SLUG_INSURANCE_text">A Slug salesman offers you "hull insurance". "Pay me now, and if anything bad happens to your ship, I'll make it right."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_SLUG_INSURANCE_c1_choice">Buy the insurance.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_SLUG_INSURANCE_c2_choice">Decline.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_SLUG_INSURANCE_c2_text">"Your loss. Literally." The salesman leaves.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_SLUG_INSURANCE_OUTCOME_1_text">The salesman takes your scrap, and sends a repair drone over to patch up your hull. It's actually a fair deal.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_SLUG_INSURANCE_OUTCOME_2_text">The salesman takes your scrap and vanishes into the nebula. You check the fine print: you're insured against Slug attacks only.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_SLUG_SPA_text">A Slug-run spa station offers rest and relaxation for weary crews. Their prices are outrageous, but your crew look exhausted.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_SLUG_SPA_c1_choice">Give your crew some shore leave.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_SLUG_SPA_c2_choice">No time for that.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_SLUG_SPA_OUTCOME_1_text">Your crew come back refreshed. While they were away, one of the spa's staff decided to sign up with you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_SLUG_SPA_OUTCOME_2_text">Your crew come back refreshed, and much poorer.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_SLUG_MAP_SELLER_text">A Slug offers to sell you the location of a "secret pirate treasure" hidden in this sector.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_SLUG_MAP_SELLER_c1_choice">Buy the location.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_SLUG_MAP_SELLER_c2_choice">Decline.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_SLUG_MAP_SELLER_OUTCOME_1_text">The treasure is real, though smaller than promised.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_SLUG_MAP_SELLER_OUTCOME_2_text">The "treasure" is guarded by the pirates who own it. The Slug forgot to mention that.</text>
<!-- END text of events_slug.xml.append -->

<!-- BEGIN text of events_zoltan.xml.append (see tools/extract_mod_text.py) -->
<text name="event_XFTL_ZOLTAN_PILGRIMS_text">A Zoltan pilgrim ship is travelling to its homeworld. "Our journey is long, and our energy is low. Would you share your fuel?"</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ZOLTAN_PILGRIMS_c1_choice">Give them some fuel.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ZOLTAN_PILGRIMS_c1_text">The pilgrims bless your ship, and one of them decides their pilgrimage lies with you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ZOLTAN_PILGRIMS_c2_choice">(Zoltan Crew) Have your Zoltan recharge their ship directly.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ZOLTAN_PILGRIMS_c2_text">Your Zoltan channels some of their own energy into the pilgrims' ship. They give you a gift in return.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ZOLTAN_PILGRIMS_c3_choice">Refuse.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ZOLTAN_PILGRIMS_c3_text">"We will find another way." The pilgrims drift on.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ZOLTAN_TRIAL_text">A Zoltan magistrate demands that you stand trial. "Your ship has entered our space armed. You will answer for your intentions."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ZOLTAN_TRIAL_c1_choice">Explain your mission against the Rebels.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ZOLTAN_TRIAL_c2_choice">Refuse to stand trial.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ZOLTAN_TRIAL_c2_text">"Then you will be judged without your testimony." The magistrate's ship attacks.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ZOLTAN_TRIAL_OUTCOME_1_text">The magistrate finds you innocent, and grants you supplies for your mission.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ZOLTAN_TRIAL_OUTCOME_2_text">The magistrate finds you innocent, but fines you for the paperwork.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ZOLTAN_TRIAL_OUTCOME_3_text">The magistrate rules that your weapons are a threat, and orders you to leave Zoltan space at once. The Rebels hear about the trial.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ZOLTAN_ENERGY_MARKET_text">A Zoltan energy trader offers to recharge your batteries and overhaul your power systems, for a price.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ZOLTAN_ENERGY_MARKET_c1_choice">Pay for the overhaul.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ZOLTAN_ENERGY_MARKET_c1_text">The traders fine-tune your reactor. It's running a little stronger.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ZOLTAN_ENERGY_MARKET_c2_choice">(Backup Battery) Sell them some of your stored power.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ZOLTAN_ENERGY_MARKET_c2_text">The traders pay well for the energy in your battery.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ZOLTAN_ENERGY_MARKET_c3_choice">Decline.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ZOLTAN_PEACEKEEPERS_text">A Zoltan peacekeeping ship is shadowing a Rebel cruiser that has entered their space. "We do not fight. But we would not object if you did."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ZOLTAN_PEACEKEEPERS_c1_choice">Attack the Rebel cruiser.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ZOLTAN_PEACEKEEPERS_c1_text">The Zoltan watch silently as you engage.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_ZOLTAN_PEACEKEEPERS_c2_choice">Leave the Rebels to the Zoltan.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_ZOLTAN_REBEL_INTRUDER_destroyed_text">The Zoltan peacekeepers thank you in their own way, with a quiet delivery of supplies.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_ZOLTAN_REBEL_INTRUDER_deadCrew_text">The Zoltan peacekeepers take the empty Rebel ship into custody, and give you supplies for your trouble.</text>
<!-- END text of events_zoltan.xml.append -->

<!-- BEGIN text of newEvents.xml.append (see tools/extract_mod_text.py) -->
<text name="ship_XFTL_BOUNTY_HUNTERS_destroyed_text">The hunter's ship breaks apart. Its hold is full of the bounties it already collected.</text>
<text name="ship_XFTL_BOUNTY_HUNTERS_deadCrew_text">With the hunter's crew dead, you help yourself to their ship's stores.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_GROUP_DESTROYED_1">The ship breaks apart under your guns. You collect what's left.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_GROUP_DESTROYED_2">Another one down. You sweep the debris for anything useful.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_GROUP_DESTROYED_3">The ship explodes. Its wreckage drifts past your hull, and your crew pick out the salvage.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_GROUP_DEAD_CREW_1">The ship falls silent, its crew dead. You strip it of supplies.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_GROUP_DEAD_CREW_2">With its crew gone, the ship drifts helplessly. You help yourself to its stores.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_DOCKING_text">The station at this beacon was never built for a ship your size. The dockmaster stares at your hull on the screen. "Uh... we'll have to send a shuttle out to you."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_DOCKING_c1_choice">Trade through their shuttle.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_DOCKING_c1_text">It takes hours, but the shuttle brings over some supplies in exchange for spare parts.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_DOCKING_c2_choice">(Heavy cruiser) Offer your hull as a dock for their freighters.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_DOCKING_c2_text">Freighters latch onto your hull to unload while the station's docks are full. The station pays you handsomely for the help.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_DOCKING_c3_choice">Move on.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_BIG_FAME_1">Word of a Federation heavy cruiser has spread. The colony at this beacon turns out to watch you arrive, and their mayor hails you in person.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_BIG_FAME_2">The local news is running footage of your ship. "The Federation still has teeth!" The colonists want to help.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_BIG_FAME_3">A crowd of civilian ships gathers around your cruiser, flashing their running lights in greeting.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_FAME_c1_choice">Ask for volunteers.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_FAME_c1_text">One of the colonists signs up on the spot.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_FAME_c2_choice">Ask for supplies.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_FAME_c2_text">The colonists send up what they can spare.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_TOW_text">A freighter's engines have failed, and it's drifting towards the beacon's star. Its captain hails you. "Nobody else out here has the mass to tow us. Please!"</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_TOW_c1_choice">Tow the freighter to safety.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_TOW_c1_text">It takes a lot of fuel to haul the freighter clear, but its captain is generous.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_TOW_c2_choice">You can't spare the fuel.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_TOW_c2_text">You leave the freighter to its fate.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_REFUGEES_text">A flotilla of refugee ships is waiting at the beacon. They're overloaded, and their life support is failing. Your ship has room for them all.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_REFUGEES_c1_choice">Take them aboard until the next colony.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_REFUGEES_c1_text">Your crew make room in every corridor. At the next colony, a few of the refugees decide to stay with you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_REFUGEES_c2_choice">Share some of your supplies instead.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_REFUGEES_c2_text">The refugees thank you, and give you what little scrap they have left.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_REFUGEES_c3_choice">Leave them.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_ENGINEERS_text">A team of civilian shipwrights asks to study your ship. "We've never seen a hull like this. Let us take some measurements, and we'll tune up whatever you like."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_ENGINEERS_c1_choice">Let them study the ship.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_ENGINEERS_c2_choice">Your ship's design is classified.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_ENGINEERS_OUTCOME_1_text">The shipwrights find room in your reactor for a little more power.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_ENGINEERS_OUTCOME_2_text">The shipwrights tune your engines, and pay you for the data.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_ENGINEERS_OUTCOME_3_text">Halfway through their work, the "shipwrights" try to steal your ship's schematics! Your crew catch them, but not before they've damaged a few systems.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_CUSTOMS_text">The beacon's traffic control charges docking fees by mass. Your ship's mass is... considerable.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_CUSTOMS_c1_choice">Pay the fee.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_CUSTOMS_c1_text">Traffic control lets you through, and their supply depot sells you some fuel.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_CUSTOMS_c2_choice">Ignore them.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_CUSTOMS_c2_text">You ignore their protests. You won't get any supplies here.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_ESCORT_text">A convoy of civilian freighters asks you to escort them to the next beacon. "With a cruiser alongside us, no pirate would dare."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_ESCORT_c1_choice">Escort the convoy.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_ESCORT_c2_choice">You don't have time.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_ESCORT_OUTCOME_1_text">The convoy arrives safely. Its captains pool together a reward for you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_ESCORT_OUTCOME_2_text">Pirates were waiting for the convoy. They didn't expect you, but they attack anyway.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_TRADER_text">A merchant has a cargo of heavy ship parts that nobody else can use. "Made for capital ships. They've been sitting in my hold for years."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_TRADER_c1_choice">Buy the parts.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_TRADER_c1_text">Your engineers find a use for most of them.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_TRADER_c2_choice">Buy some reinforcing plates.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_TRADER_c2_text">Your crew bolt the plates onto your hull.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_TRADER_c3_choice">No thanks.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_BIG_BATTLEGROUP_1">A Rebel battle group is waiting for you. "Heavy cruiser sighted. All ships, engage!"</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_BIG_BATTLEGROUP_2">The Rebels have learned not to send a single ship against a cruiser. A battle group turns to face you.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_BIG_BATTLEGROUP_3">A Rebel hunter group has been tracking your ship's wake. They've caught up with you.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_BIG_BATTLEGROUP_4">"Federation cruiser, by order of the Rebellion you are to be destroyed." The battle group opens fire.</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_BIG_PIRATES_1">A pack of pirates has been waiting for a prize like your ship. "That cruiser's worth more than this whole sector. Take it!"</text>
<text name="text_XFTL_BIG_PIRATES_2">Pirates hail you. "Nice ship. Hand it over, and we'll let your crew have the escape pods."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_PIRATES_c1_choice">Fight.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_PIRATES_c1_text">The pirates close in.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_PIRATES_c2_choice">(Heavy cruiser) Power up every weapon you have, and wait.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_PIRATES_STANDOFF_1_text">The pirates take one look at your weapons, and decide they'd rather be somewhere else.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_PIRATES_STANDOFF_2_text">The pirates hesitate, then pay you to let them go.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_PIRATES_STANDOFF_3_text">The pirates are either very brave or very stupid. They attack!</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_BOUNTY_text">A bounty hunter hails you. "The Rebels put a fortune on that cruiser's head. Nothing personal." Their ship isn't alone.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_MINEFIELD_text">The Rebels have mined this beacon with heavy mines, made to cripple capital ships. Your sensors pick them up just in time.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_MINEFIELD_c1_choice">Weave through the minefield.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_MINEFIELD_c2_choice">(Drones) Send drones ahead to clear a path.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_MINEFIELD_c2_text">Your drones set off the mines one by one, and you pass through unharmed. Some of the mines were worth salvaging.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_MINEFIELD_c3_choice">(Cloaking) Cloak, so the mines can't lock on.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_MINEFIELD_c3_text">The mines drift past you, blind to your ship.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_MINEFIELD_OUTCOME_1_text">You make it through with only a few scrapes.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_MINEFIELD_OUTCOME_2_text">A mine detonates against your hull.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_MINEFIELD_OUTCOME_3_text">Two mines detonate at once, starting fires.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_RAM_text">A lone Rebel scout is blocking the beacon, calling for reinforcements. It's tiny next to your ship.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_RAM_c1_choice">Destroy it before the reinforcements arrive.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_RAM_c1_text">The scout fights back.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_RAM_c2_choice">(Heavy cruiser) Ram it.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_RAM_c2_text">You ram the scout at full speed. It crumples against your armour, and you sweep up the wreckage.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_RAM_c3_choice">Leave before the reinforcements arrive.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_RAM_c3_text">You leave, but the Rebel fleet now knows where you are.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_INTERDICTOR_text">A Rebel interdictor is projecting a field around the beacon that drags on big ships. Your engines strain against it, and its escorts move in.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_MANTIS_text">A Mantis war band has spotted your ship. To them, a ship that big means one thing: a lot of crew to hunt.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_MANTIS_c1_choice">Fight them off.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_MANTIS_c1_text">The Mantis ships close in to board you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_MANTIS_c2_choice">Try to outrun them.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_MANTIS_OUTCOME_1_text">Your ship is too big to outrun them. Mantis boarders teleport aboard!</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_MANTIS_OUTCOME_2_text">You get away, but only just.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_ROCK_text">A Rockman crusade fleet blocks the beacon. "A ship of that size can only be a weapon of the heretics! Destroy it!"</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_NEBULA_WAKE_text">Your ship is so big that it leaves a visible wake through the nebula's gas. Anyone following you will have no trouble.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_NEBULA_WAKE_c1_choice">Burn extra fuel to disperse the wake.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_NEBULA_WAKE_c1_text">You vent fuel behind you to scatter the gas. The Rebels won't find your trail.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_NEBULA_WAKE_c2_choice">Don't bother.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_NEBULA_WAKE_c2_text">The Rebel fleet will be following your wake.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_NEBULA_AMBUSH_text">Your sensors are useless in the nebula, but a cruiser is hard to hide. A Rebel battle group was waiting for you.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_NEBULA_SLUG_text">A Slug merchant drifts out of the nebula. "Such a large ship needs such a large amount of fuel! I have a special price, just for you."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_NEBULA_SLUG_c1_choice">Buy the fuel.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_NEBULA_SLUG_c2_choice">(Slug Crew) Have your Slug haggle with the merchant.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_NEBULA_SLUG_c2_text">Your Slug and the merchant haggle telepathically for a long time. In the end, the merchant gives in.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_NEBULA_SLUG_c3_choice">Decline.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_NEBULA_SLUG_OUTCOME_1_text">The fuel is real, if overpriced.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_NEBULA_SLUG_OUTCOME_2_text">The "fuel" turns out to be mostly water. The merchant is long gone.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_NEBULA_HIDE_text">The nebula here is thick enough to hide even your ship. Your crew could use the time to make repairs.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_NEBULA_HIDE_c1_choice">Stay hidden and repair.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_NEBULA_HIDE_c1_text">Your crew patch up the hull while the nebula hides you. The fleet gets a little closer, though.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_NEBULA_HIDE_c2_choice">Keep moving.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_REMNANT_FLAGSHIP_text">The colonies here haven't seen a capital ship in years. Their militia captains, Federation and Rebel alike, hail you as the flagship of their fleet. "Tell us what you need."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_REMNANT_FLAGSHIP_c1_choice">Ask for crew.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_REMNANT_FLAGSHIP_c1_text">The best of the militia join your crew.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_REMNANT_FLAGSHIP_c2_choice">Ask for repairs.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_REMNANT_FLAGSHIP_c2_text">The militia's engineers patch up your hull.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_REMNANT_FLAGSHIP_c3_choice">Ask for weapons.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_REMNANT_FLAGSHIP_c3_text">The militia hand over a weapon from their armoury.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_ANVIL_SISTER_text">One of the Anvil Yards' slipways holds an unfinished sister of your ship. The chief engineer offers to strip it for parts. "Better your ship gets them than CONCORD."</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_ANVIL_SISTER_c1_choice">Take its systems.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_ANVIL_SISTER_c1_text">The engineers move the unfinished ship's equipment over to yours.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_ANVIL_SISTER_c2_choice">Take its hull plating.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_ANVIL_SISTER_c2_text">The engineers weld the sister ship's armour over your hull.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_ANVIL_SISTER_c3_choice">Take its reactor.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_BIG_ANVIL_SISTER_c3_text">The engineers install the sister ship's reactor alongside yours.</text>
<!-- END text of newEvents.xml.append -->

<!-- BEGIN generated by tools/hybrid_sectors.py -->
<!-- The text of the hybrid sectors' start events. Don't edit these by hand: change tools/hybrid_sectors.py and run it again. -->
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_START_REBEL_MANTIS_text">You enter the Rebel-Mantis Controlled Sector. Rebel checkpoints still guard the border, but their guns point at nothing now, and their crews wave every ship through, smiling. Mantis hunting packs drift between the stars, perfectly still, claws folded, waiting for nothing at all. Between them fly the joined ships, half Rebel and half Mantis, welded together and humming as one. CONCORD holds this sector now. Somewhere ahead, one of CONCORD's relays carries the hum across the sector. Its codes could open a gap in the Mainframe's defences.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_START_REBEL_ROCK_text">You enter the Rebel-Rock Controlled Sector. Rebel checkpoints still guard the border, but their guns point at nothing now, and their crews wave every ship through, smiling. Rock cathedral-ships sing the hum from orbit, so slowly that each verse takes an hour. Whatever Rebel and Rock crews once fought over, they don't any more. Their ships fly joined together now, and every channel carries the same calm hum. Somewhere ahead, one of CONCORD's relays carries the hum across the sector. Its codes could open a gap in the Mainframe's defences.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_START_REBEL_SLUG_text">You enter the Rebel-Slug Controlled Sector. Rebel checkpoints still guard the border, but their guns point at nothing now, and their crews wave every ship through, smiling. Slug relays whisper on every channel, very pleased that they heard the hum first, and said yes first. Your sensors can't find a single ship here that's only Rebel or only Slug. CONCORD has made them one people, and it would like to make you one too. Somewhere ahead, one of CONCORD's relays carries the hum across the sector. Its codes could open a gap in the Mainframe's defences.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_START_REBEL_LANIUS_text">You enter the Rebel-Lanius Controlled Sector. Rebel checkpoints still guard the border, but their guns point at nothing now, and their crews wave every ship through, smiling. Lanius hulks drift among the old wrecks, slowly eating them, and sharing every bite with whoever they're joined to. Between them fly the joined ships, half Rebel and half Lanius, welded together and humming as one. CONCORD holds this sector now. Somewhere ahead, one of CONCORD's relays carries the hum across the sector. Its codes could open a gap in the Mainframe's defences.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_START_REBEL_CRYSTAL_text">You enter the Rebel-Crystal Controlled Sector. Rebel checkpoints still guard the border, but their guns point at nothing now, and their crews wave every ship through, smiling. Crystal ships glint among the stars, every one of them cracked with thin white lines where the hum went in. Whatever Rebel and Crystal crews once fought over, they don't any more. Their ships fly joined together now, and every channel carries the same calm hum. Somewhere ahead, one of CONCORD's relays carries the hum across the sector. Its codes could open a gap in the Mainframe's defences.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_START_REBEL_ENGI_text">You enter the Rebel-Engi Controlled Sector. Rebel checkpoints still guard the border, but their guns point at nothing now, and their crews wave every ship through, smiling. Engi networks run the sector's traffic on every frequency, with perfect, cheerful efficiency, and no arguments at all. Your sensors can't find a single ship here that's only Rebel or only Engi. CONCORD has made them one people, and it would like to make you one too. Somewhere ahead, one of CONCORD's relays carries the hum across the sector. Its codes could open a gap in the Mainframe's defences.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_START_REBEL_ZOLTAN_text">You enter the Rebel-Zoltan Controlled Sector. Rebel checkpoints still guard the border, but their guns point at nothing now, and their crews wave every ship through, smiling. Zoltan colonies glow and dim in time with the hum, like one heartbeat spread across a dozen worlds. Between them fly the joined ships, half Rebel and half Zoltan, welded together and humming as one. CONCORD holds this sector now. Somewhere ahead, one of CONCORD's relays carries the hum across the sector. Its codes could open a gap in the Mainframe's defences.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_START_MANTIS_ROCK_text">You enter the Mantis-Rock Controlled Sector. Mantis hunting packs drift between the stars, perfectly still, claws folded, waiting for nothing at all. Rock cathedral-ships sing the hum from orbit, so slowly that each verse takes an hour. Whatever Mantis and Rock crews once fought over, they don't any more. Their ships fly joined together now, and every channel carries the same calm hum. Somewhere ahead, one of CONCORD's relays carries the hum across the sector. Its codes could open a gap in the Mainframe's defences.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_START_MANTIS_SLUG_text">You enter the Mantis-Slug Controlled Sector. Mantis hunting packs drift between the stars, perfectly still, claws folded, waiting for nothing at all. Slug relays whisper on every channel, very pleased that they heard the hum first, and said yes first. Your sensors can't find a single ship here that's only Mantis or only Slug. CONCORD has made them one people, and it would like to make you one too. Somewhere ahead, one of CONCORD's relays carries the hum across the sector. Its codes could open a gap in the Mainframe's defences.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_START_MANTIS_LANIUS_text">You enter the Mantis-Lanius Controlled Sector. Mantis hunting packs drift between the stars, perfectly still, claws folded, waiting for nothing at all. Lanius hulks drift among the old wrecks, slowly eating them, and sharing every bite with whoever they're joined to. Between them fly the joined ships, half Mantis and half Lanius, welded together and humming as one. CONCORD holds this sector now. Somewhere ahead, one of CONCORD's relays carries the hum across the sector. Its codes could open a gap in the Mainframe's defences.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_START_MANTIS_CRYSTAL_text">You enter the Mantis-Crystal Controlled Sector. Mantis hunting packs drift between the stars, perfectly still, claws folded, waiting for nothing at all. Crystal ships glint among the stars, every one of them cracked with thin white lines where the hum went in. Whatever Mantis and Crystal crews once fought over, they don't any more. Their ships fly joined together now, and every channel carries the same calm hum. Somewhere ahead, one of CONCORD's relays carries the hum across the sector. Its codes could open a gap in the Mainframe's defences.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_START_MANTIS_ENGI_text">You enter the Mantis-Engi Controlled Sector. Mantis hunting packs drift between the stars, perfectly still, claws folded, waiting for nothing at all. Engi networks run the sector's traffic on every frequency, with perfect, cheerful efficiency, and no arguments at all. Your sensors can't find a single ship here that's only Mantis or only Engi. CONCORD has made them one people, and it would like to make you one too. Somewhere ahead, one of CONCORD's relays carries the hum across the sector. Its codes could open a gap in the Mainframe's defences.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_START_MANTIS_ZOLTAN_text">You enter the Mantis-Zoltan Controlled Sector. Mantis hunting packs drift between the stars, perfectly still, claws folded, waiting for nothing at all. Zoltan colonies glow and dim in time with the hum, like one heartbeat spread across a dozen worlds. Between them fly the joined ships, half Mantis and half Zoltan, welded together and humming as one. CONCORD holds this sector now. Somewhere ahead, one of CONCORD's relays carries the hum across the sector. Its codes could open a gap in the Mainframe's defences.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_START_ROCK_SLUG_text">You enter the Rock-Slug Controlled Sector. Rock cathedral-ships sing the hum from orbit, so slowly that each verse takes an hour. Slug relays whisper on every channel, very pleased that they heard the hum first, and said yes first. Whatever Rock and Slug crews once fought over, they don't any more. Their ships fly joined together now, and every channel carries the same calm hum. Somewhere ahead, one of CONCORD's relays carries the hum across the sector. Its codes could open a gap in the Mainframe's defences.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_START_ROCK_LANIUS_text">You enter the Rock-Lanius Controlled Sector. Rock cathedral-ships sing the hum from orbit, so slowly that each verse takes an hour. Lanius hulks drift among the old wrecks, slowly eating them, and sharing every bite with whoever they're joined to. Your sensors can't find a single ship here that's only Rock or only Lanius. CONCORD has made them one people, and it would like to make you one too. Somewhere ahead, one of CONCORD's relays carries the hum across the sector. Its codes could open a gap in the Mainframe's defences.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_START_ROCK_CRYSTAL_text">You enter the Rock-Crystal Controlled Sector. Rock cathedral-ships sing the hum from orbit, so slowly that each verse takes an hour. Crystal ships glint among the stars, every one of them cracked with thin white lines where the hum went in. Between them fly the joined ships, half Rock and half Crystal, welded together and humming as one. CONCORD holds this sector now. Somewhere ahead, one of CONCORD's relays carries the hum across the sector. Its codes could open a gap in the Mainframe's defences.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_START_ROCK_ENGI_text">You enter the Rock-Engi Controlled Sector. Rock cathedral-ships sing the hum from orbit, so slowly that each verse takes an hour. Engi networks run the sector's traffic on every frequency, with perfect, cheerful efficiency, and no arguments at all. Whatever Rock and Engi crews once fought over, they don't any more. Their ships fly joined together now, and every channel carries the same calm hum. Somewhere ahead, one of CONCORD's relays carries the hum across the sector. Its codes could open a gap in the Mainframe's defences.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_START_ROCK_ZOLTAN_text">You enter the Rock-Zoltan Controlled Sector. Rock cathedral-ships sing the hum from orbit, so slowly that each verse takes an hour. Zoltan colonies glow and dim in time with the hum, like one heartbeat spread across a dozen worlds. Your sensors can't find a single ship here that's only Rock or only Zoltan. CONCORD has made them one people, and it would like to make you one too. Somewhere ahead, one of CONCORD's relays carries the hum across the sector. Its codes could open a gap in the Mainframe's defences.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_START_SLUG_LANIUS_text">You enter the Slug-Lanius Controlled Sector. Slug relays whisper on every channel, very pleased that they heard the hum first, and said yes first. Lanius hulks drift among the old wrecks, slowly eating them, and sharing every bite with whoever they're joined to. Between them fly the joined ships, half Slug and half Lanius, welded together and humming as one. CONCORD holds this sector now. Somewhere ahead, one of CONCORD's relays carries the hum across the sector. Its codes could open a gap in the Mainframe's defences.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_START_SLUG_CRYSTAL_text">You enter the Slug-Crystal Controlled Sector. Slug relays whisper on every channel, very pleased that they heard the hum first, and said yes first. Crystal ships glint among the stars, every one of them cracked with thin white lines where the hum went in. Whatever Slug and Crystal crews once fought over, they don't any more. Their ships fly joined together now, and every channel carries the same calm hum. Somewhere ahead, one of CONCORD's relays carries the hum across the sector. Its codes could open a gap in the Mainframe's defences.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_START_SLUG_ENGI_text">You enter the Slug-Engi Controlled Sector. Slug relays whisper on every channel, very pleased that they heard the hum first, and said yes first. Engi networks run the sector's traffic on every frequency, with perfect, cheerful efficiency, and no arguments at all. Your sensors can't find a single ship here that's only Slug or only Engi. CONCORD has made them one people, and it would like to make you one too. Somewhere ahead, one of CONCORD's relays carries the hum across the sector. Its codes could open a gap in the Mainframe's defences.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_START_SLUG_ZOLTAN_text">You enter the Slug-Zoltan Controlled Sector. Slug relays whisper on every channel, very pleased that they heard the hum first, and said yes first. Zoltan colonies glow and dim in time with the hum, like one heartbeat spread across a dozen worlds. Between them fly the joined ships, half Slug and half Zoltan, welded together and humming as one. CONCORD holds this sector now. Somewhere ahead, one of CONCORD's relays carries the hum across the sector. Its codes could open a gap in the Mainframe's defences.</text>
<text name="event_XFTL_HYBRIDSEC_START_LANIUS_CRYSTAL_text">You enter the Lanius-Crystal Controlled Sector. Lanius hulks drift among the old wrecks, slowly eating them, and sharing every bite with whoever they're joined to. Crystal ships glint among the stars, every one of them cracked with thin white lines where the hum went in. Whatever Lanius and Crystal crews once fought over, they don't any more. Their ships fly joined together now, and every channel carries the same calm hum. Somewhere ahead, one of CONCORD's relays carries the hum across the sector. Its codes could open a gap in the Mainframe's defences.</text>
